id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gs-layer","id":263342938,"login":"gs-layer","node_id":"U_kgDOD7JLWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commits/c65d3035503107f24b27be2baa2a5138c92ed7ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:46:40Z","email":"grigoriis.dev@gmail.com","name":"G S"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T02:43:56Z","email":"246844849+GeraBart@users.noreply.github.com","name":"GeraBart"},"message":"feat(template-shell): declare shell domain routes and the entry-addresses shared property\n\nSigned-off-by: G S <grigoriis.dev@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec0d7ee8a43a79eace439b91264acb4281c3f90c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/git/trees/ec0d7ee8a43a79eace439b91264acb4281c3f90c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/git/commits/c65d3035503107f24b27be2baa2a5138c92ed7ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","id":246844849,"login":"GeraBart","node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commit/c65d3035503107f24b27be2baa2a5138c92ed7ae","node_id":"C_kwDOTn9Ds9oAKGM2NWQzMDM1NTAzMTA3ZjI0YjI3YmUyYmFhMmE1MTM4YzkyZWQ3YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commit/e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941","sha":"e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commits/e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941"}],"sha":"c65d3035503107f24b27be2baa2a5138c92ed7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commits/c65d3035503107f24b27be2baa2a5138c92ed7ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263342938?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gs-layer","id":263342938,"login":"gs-layer","node_id":"U_kgDOD7JLWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gs-layer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commits/e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:28:44Z","email":"grigoriis.dev@gmail.com","name":"G S"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T02:43:56Z","email":"246844849+GeraBart@users.noreply.github.com","name":"GeraBart"},"message":"chore(deps): bump @gears-frontx/framework and pin routing packages for declared routes\n\nBump @gears-frontx/framework from 0.2.0-alpha.8 to 0.2.0-alpha.9 and\n@gears-frontx/gts-plugin / @gears-frontx/mfes from 0.3.0-alpha.7 to\n0.3.0-alpha.8 across template-shell and the mfe fixtures, and add\n@gears-frontx/routing at 0.3.0-alpha.0 as a template-shell dependency\nso the shell can declare routes (#638).\n\nSigned-off-by: G S <grigoriis.dev@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"198cea71dfa5e283d2068bc89cc03ac821972578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/git/trees/198cea71dfa5e283d2068bc89cc03ac821972578"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/git/commits/e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","id":246844849,"login":"GeraBart","node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commit/e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941","node_id":"C_kwDOTn9Ds9oAKGU5MDUyYjkzMzE0MTkxZGU2NjNiY2YwZDMwYjA1N2IyYzM2YjE5NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commit/65685ae749f503965b7d0aa6a22498fd1da48f4a","sha":"65685ae749f503965b7d0aa6a22498fd1da48f4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commits/65685ae749f503965b7d0aa6a22498fd1da48f4a"}],"sha":"e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commits/e9052b93314191de663bcf0d30b057b2c36b1941"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225432371?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tscbmstubp","id":225432371,"login":"tscbmstubp","node_id":"U_kgDODW_TMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tscbmstubp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/commits/65685ae749f503965b7d0aa6a22498fd1da48f4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:19:29Z","email":"davydowiktor@gmail.com","name":"Vuk D."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T06:38:21Z","email":"246844849+GeraBart@users.noreply.github.com","name":"GeraBart"},"message":"feat: import template-shell, template-mfe, and template-design-guardrails from gears-frontx\n\nThe FrontX templates, split out of gears-frontx into their own repository.\nThis repo holds nothing but templates, the CI guards that keep them\nconsistent with the FrontX ecosystem, and the tooling those guards need -\nnot a workspace over the templates (each keeps its own package.json and\nlockfile) and no packages/* of its own.\n\n## What moved\n\nVerbatim copies (git ls-files in the source repo) of all three templates,\ndirectory names unchanged - the CLI addresses them by subtree\n(github:constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates//<template>@<ref>,\nADR-0017). Git history stays in gears-frontx. Originally split at commit\na08c2539; resynced once already to 1531fba3 after gears-frontx develop\nmoved on (9 commits, 31 files under template-shell/ and template-mfe/ -\nsee \"Resync to 1531fba3\" below).\n\nAlso moved: the template half of gears-frontx''s repo-scripts (template\ndiscovery, prepublish manifest+content validation, ecosystem pin-drift,\nlockfile self-link, token-format, guideline-index, and the template half of\nversion-bump-on-change - the packages/* half stayed in gears-frontx), and\nscripts/manual-auth-tests/ (hand-run auth() integration demos gears-frontx\ncould no longer build once template-shell, which they import\n@gears-frontx/framework from, left).\n\n## What had to change, and why\n\nThere is no local packages/* here any more, so:\n\n- template-ecosystem-packages.mjs''s pin-drift truth map has two modes:\n  FRONTX_ECOSYSTEM_DIR set -> read packages/*/package.json from that sibling\n  gears-frontx checkout and require exact matches (sibling mode); unset ->\n  verify each pinned @gears-frontx/* package directly against the npm\n  registry via `npm view` (registry mode), failing closed on an unplaceable\n  name or a nonexistent version. The @gears-frontx scope itself bootstraps\n  from the templates'' own manifests when there''s no local packages/* to\n  derive it from. Sibling mode also fails closed on zero packages/*\n  discovered (a bad FRONTX_ECOSYSTEM_DIR used to pass vacuously), registry\n  mode distinguishes an npm-view E404 (a real \"not found\") from any other\n  npm/network failure (rethrown as a distinct infra error), and both modes\n  now cover this repo''s own root package.json pins, not just the templates''.\n- link-template-ecosystem.mjs and pin-template-ecosystem-to-local.mjs take\n  the ecosystem root from FRONTX_ECOSYSTEM_DIR (default ../gears-frontx\n  sibling) instead of assuming this repo''s own root.\n- version-bump-on-change-check.mjs''s packages/* discovery degrades\n  gracefully to empty, so governance falls through entirely to\n  template-shell and its workspace members; default base ref is now\n  origin/main (this repo has one branch, unlike the monorepo''s\n  develop/main/release model).\n- template-mfe/package.json drops its three overrides into\n  ../packages/{api,gts-plugin,mfes} (paths that only exist in the ecosystem\n  repo) - those three now resolve from the registry via their exact pins,\n  verified end-to-end (api/gts-plugin/mfes install as real tarballs;\n  auth/framework/i18n/react/state/frontx-template-shell still symlink to the\n  sibling template-shell/). Its lockfile is regenerated to match.\n- manual-auth-tests moved into template-shell/manual-auth-tests/ (a new\n  top-level directory, deliberately outside ownershipBoundaries so no\n  seeded project ever receives it) rather than under gears-frontx''s old\n  scripts/ location, because that''s what makes @gears-frontx/framework\n  resolve: after npm ci + npm run build:packages in template-shell/, it''s a\n  workspace member hoisted to node_modules/@gears-frontx/framework. Verified\n  end-to-end against the real DummyJSON backend.\n- Two cross-repo test guards (comparing this repo''s literals against\n  packages/cli source files) were dropped - neither the comparison nor the\n  obligation moved to gears-frontx (that repo has no way to see a literal\n  declared here); the practical mitigation is validate-templates.mjs, which\n  never reads either local literal and checks the real manifests through the\n  installed CLI directly instead.\n\n## Root tooling added\n\npackage.json (private, not a workspace) exposing the moved scripts, pinned\nto vitest@4.1.4 and @gears-frontx/cli@0.3.0-alpha.4 - the alpha dist-tag,\nnot the stale \"latest\" (0.1.5), which predates validateCommand,\ncreateFsReadFileFn, and createFsListContentOwnedFilesFn. vitest.config.mjs\ncollects scripts/**/*.test.mjs only.\n\n.github/workflows/main.yml (validate:templates, policy:template-pin-drift in\nregistry mode, policy:template-lockfile-selflink, policy:token-format,\npolicy:guideline-index, policy:version-bump-on-change on PRs, plus\ntemplate-validate: self-contained templates validated standalone,\ntemplate-mfe composed onto template-shell and validated as a seeded project\nwould see it; workflow_dispatch for a manual run on a fork branch),\ntemplate-drift.yml (checks out gears-frontx''s develop branch into a sibling\npath - path filters can''t see a cross-repo change, so also a daily schedule\n- builds it, runs policy:template-pin-drift in sibling mode against it, then\nthe same pin-to-local + relink + build/type-check sequence the local dev\nloop does), and publish-packages.yml (the shell template + its subpackages,\ndependency-ordered, version-gated; must run after the ecosystem packages a\nbumped pin here names are themselves published on gears-frontx; documents\nits NPM_TOKEN secret requirement and its safe-by-construction first-run\nbehavior). README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md document the source-spec, the\nFRONTX_ECOSYSTEM_DIR env var and its two default behaviours, and the dev\nloop against a sibling gears-frontx checkout.\n\n## Resync to 1531fba3\n\ngears-frontx develop moved on since the a08c2539 split base. Re-synced\nevery git-tracked path under template-shell/ and template-mfe/ to\n1531fba3 (template-design-guardrails untouched) - 9 commits, 31 files:\n\n- react: useSharedProperty gains an explicit-bridge form (#570); the mfe\n  hooks barrel, index re-exports, CLAUDE.md, llms.txt, and the mfe hooks\n  test all updated to match.\n- demo-mfe: bridge-property and RTL-direction logic extracted into shared\n  hooks (useBridgeProperty, useHostDirection, with their own tests) and\n  reused across all four demo screens (#502).\n- Pin bumps across template-shell''s packages/* and every template-mfe\n  fixture: @gears-frontx/api 0.3.0-alpha.1->2, gts-plugin and mfes\n  alpha.3->4, react alpha.5->7, framework alpha.4->5, auth alpha.1->2,\n  state and i18n alpha.0->1 - plus third-party bumps (typescript 5.9.3,\n  tsup 8.5.1, @reduxjs/toolkit 2.12.0, and others) and both lockfiles\n  resynced to match.\n\nEvery non-lockfile path was verified byte-identical to\n`git show origin/develop:<path>` after the sync. Kept both intentional\ndeltas as-is: template-mfe/package.json (no ../packages/{api,gts-plugin,\nmfes} overrides - unchanged upstream, so no edit needed) and\ntemplate-shell/manual-auth-tests/ (not part of gears-frontx at all).\ntemplate-mfe/package-lock.json was regenerated fresh rather than copied,\nto reflect its still-overridden pins alongside the newly bumped registry\nones - verified after regeneration that api/gts-plugin/mfes still resolve\nas real registry tarballs at their new versions while react/auth/\nframework/i18n/state/frontx-template-shell still symlink to the sibling\ntemplate-shell/.\n\n## Root manifest pins are always a registry question\n\nA fork dry run of template-drift.yml on the resynced commit found one false\npositive: root package.json devDependencies[\"@gears-frontx/cli\"] pinned\n0.3.0-alpha.4, reported as drifted because gears-frontx develop''s own\npackages/cli had moved to 0.3.0-alpha.5. That comparison was wrong by\ndesign - the root manifest''s @gears-frontx/cli devDependency installs the\n*published* CLI so validate-templates.mjs can run it; it cannot follow an\nunpublished develop version (npm ci would fail on it), and it is not a\ntemplate pin site at all.\n\nThe root manifest''s own pins are now verified against the registry\nunconditionally, in BOTH modes (found/E404 vs a rethrown infra error, same\nrule template pins already used in registry mode) - never compared against\nsibling-checkout truth. Template pin sites are unaffected: sibling mode\nstill does exact-match-against-checkout, registry mode still does\nexists-on-registry. The zero-templates and zero-ecosystem-packages\nfail-closed floors are unchanged. Module docblocks\n(template-pin-drift-check.mjs, template-ecosystem-packages.mjs''s\nresolveEcosystemMode) and the README sentence describing what each mode\nchecks now say this explicitly.\n\n## Verification\n\nnpm ci at the root: npm test (218/218), validate:templates,\npolicy:template-pin-drift (registry mode - every new pinned version,\nincluding @gears-frontx/api@0.3.0-alpha.2, gts-plugin and mfes@0.3.0-\nalpha.4, and react@0.2.0-alpha.7, confirmed to exist on the real npm\nregistry; sibling mode checked against a synthetic checkout matching this\nrepo''s real pins, AND for real against /home/viktor/gears-frontx-externalize\n- packages/cli@0.3.0-alpha.6, no template dirs, api/gts-plugin/mfes\nmatching develop - which now passes clean on the root pin), policy:\ntemplate-lockfile-selflink, policy:token-format, and policy:guideline-index\nall pass. In template-shell/: npm ci, build, type-check, lint, arch:deps,\nand test:unit (686/686 - +8 from the explicit-bridge form''s new hooks\ntests) all pass. manual-auth-tests/ re-verified against the real DummyJSON\nbackend with the new pins in place. The MFE overlay composition\ntemplate-validate''s second job performs was reproduced by hand -\ntemplate-mfe''s 4 fixture packages composed onto a template-shell copy,\ninstall, build, type-check, arch:deps, lint, and test:unit all green with\nall 4 MFEs building and type-checking.\n\n## template-drift.yml: esbuild was an undeclared direct import\n\nA fork dry run of template-drift.yml on the resynced commit got past main.yml\nand the new sibling pin-drift step clean, but failed later in \"Build\ntemplate against the gears-frontx checkout\": tsup''s DTS build of\ntemplate-shell errored on `src/build/mf-gts.ts(1,26): Cannot find module\n''esbuild''`. The same workflow passes upstream in gears-frontx on develop.\n\nDiagnosis, confirmed by reproducing the drift sequence locally against\n/home/viktor/gears-frontx-externalize as the sibling (pin-to-local, `npm\ninstall --no-package-lock`, restore, dev:template:link, build): mf-gts.ts\nimports esbuild directly, but template-shell/package.json only ever\ndeclared it as an OPTIONAL peer dependency - never a real dependency or\ndevDependency. npm does not auto-install an optional peer. In the\nmonorepo, a root node_modules hoisted some transitive esbuild copy up\nregardless of that gap; here, with no parent node_modules and no lockfile\nguiding the fresh `--no-package-lock` resolution pin-to-local requires,\nnothing forces esbuild into node_modules at all. main.yml''s own `npm ci`\n(the committed, already-resolved lockfile) never hits this, which is why\nit stayed green there.\n\nChecked every other peerDependenciesMeta.optional entry across\ntemplate-shell and its workspace packages for the same gap - esbuild was\nthe only one (vite has the same optional-peer shape but is separately\ndeclared as a real devDependency; every REQUIRED peer elsewhere is either\nseparately declared or reliably auto-installed by npm regardless of\nlockfile).\n\nFix: added `\"esbuild\": \"0.28.2\"` to template-shell/package.json''s\ndevDependencies - the exact version its own peerDependencies entry already\nnamed and its lockfile already resolved under `npm ci` - and regenerated\nthe lockfile with `npm install --package-lock-only`. The self-link entry\nis untouched.\n\nVerified: reproduced the full drift sequence against\n/home/viktor/gears-frontx-externalize twice - once confirming the original\nfailure, once (after the fix) confirming build and type-check both succeed\nend to end. npm test (218/218), all five guards (including\npolicy:template-lockfile-selflink), and in template-shell/: npm ci, build,\ntype-check, lint, arch:deps, and test:unit (686/686) all still pass.\n\n## Human PR review: workflow correctness, ownership, fail-closed reads, ADR-0003 parity\n\nA human reviewer on PR 1 found:\n\n- publish-packages.yml''s detect-template hardcoded two workspace globs while\n  template-shell/package.json''s own \"workspaces\" field already had a third\n  (src-app/verify_packages/*) - a publishable package there would have been\n  silently skipped. MANIFESTS is now derived from that field directly (jq),\n  so this can''t drift again.\n- No .github/CODEOWNERS - added, carrying gears-frontx''s own owners for\n  /template-shell/ and /template-mfe/ over to all three template dirs here,\n  plus scripts/ and .github/.\n- pin-template-ecosystem-to-local.mjs''s readExistingOverrides and\n  applyPinLocalization both bypassed the fail-closed manifest-read handling\n  every other script in this repo uses, and applyPinLocalization re-read the\n  manifest from disk a second time instead of reusing the object\n  planPinLocalization already validated - risking a bare TypeError. Fixed by\n  threading the once-read, already-validated manifest object through\n  ManifestEdit, and extracting the shared \"read JSON, fail closed naming the\n  file\" primitive (readJsonFileOrThrow) that readPackageManifest now wraps -\n  the one shared implementation this repo''s manifest reads build on.\n- ADR-0003''s mfes-import-boundary guard lost its consumer-side subject when\n  template-shell moved out of gears-frontx, silently making the ADR''s\n  \"CI confirms both halves of the boundary\" claim false. Ported the\n  consumer half here (the barrel half stays in gears-frontx, where\n  packages/mfes still lives): no template directory may import a concrete\n  Default* implementation name from @gears-frontx/mfes or deep-import past\n  its barrel. New script, 45 ported tests, wired into main.yml.\n- Smaller: generate-guideline-index.mjs now uses process.exitCode instead of\n  process.exit(), matching every other script; version-bump-on-change-\n  check.mjs''s docblock now says origin/main (the code already did); removed\n  scripts/fs-types.mjs, a type-only file whose two documented consumers\n  never moved into this repo; CONTRIBUTING.md documents the runCli-\n  boilerplate and read-memoization consolidations considered and\n  deliberately skipped.\n\nVerified: npm test (267/267), all six guard scripts (including the new\npolicy:template-mfes-import-boundary) green, template-shell/''s own npm ci,\nbuild, type-check, lint, arch:deps, and test:unit (686/686) all pass, and\nthe full drift sequence reproduced end to end against\n/home/viktor/gears-frontx-externalize (pin-to-local, npm install\n--no-package-lock, restore, dev:template:link, build, type-check) - all\ngreen, confirming the manifest-read refactor didn''t disturb that flow.\n\n## Re-sync after gears-frontx#615\n\nRe-synced the template tree to gears-frontx develop e4351bc3 now that the\necosystem side (constructorfabric/gears-frontx#615) has merged: applied\n`git diff 1531fba3 e4351bc3 -- template-shell template-mfe\ntemplate-design-guardrails` (commits 9bcbdabd..e4351bc3, PRs #620 \"parallel\ndeps fetching\" and #625 \"shared dep dedup\", including c111b0f1''s mf-gts\ncontentHash generation and 1100347b''s version bump) with `git apply --3way`\ncleanly, no conflicts - our esbuild devDependency and manual-auth-tests/\nadaptations were untouched by the upstream diff. Re-pinned every exact\necosystem pin site to the versions gears-frontx''s publish-packages run\npublished on cf2bb843 (queued at task start, confirmed landed mid-task):\n@gears-frontx/mfes 0.3.0-alpha.6 -> 0.3.0-alpha.7, @gears-frontx/gts-plugin\n0.3.0-alpha.6 -> 0.3.0-alpha.7, @gears-frontx/api 0.3.0-alpha.2 ->\n0.3.0-alpha.3, @gears-frontx/cli (root devDependency) 0.3.0-alpha.4 ->\n0.3.0-alpha.6 (@gears-frontx/ui-kit was already at the target\n0.4.0-alpha.3). Regenerated template-shell/ and template-mfe/''s lockfiles\nvia `npm install`; the stale nested tsup@8.0.0 entry in\ntemplate-shell/package-lock.json is gone (`npm ls tsup` clean).\npolicy:template-pin-drift passes in registry mode.\n\nAlso addressed itechmeat''s six pre-merge review items:\n\n1. template-drift.yml''s sibling-mode pin-drift step now runs after the\n   build and type-check steps, with `continue-on-error: true` and a comment\n   explaining why (develop is expected to run ahead of the pins for the\n   whole window between an ecosystem publish and this repo''s own re-pin;\n   pin correctness is already covered on every PR by main.yml''s\n   registry-mode check).\n2. CONTRIBUTING.md, README.md, publish-packages.yml''s header/job name, and\n   scripts/version-bump-on-change-check.mjs''s own docblocks and error\n   strings now say the truth: `template-shell` itself is `\"private\": true`\n   and never published; only the six `template-shell/packages/*` workspace\n   members are governed/publishable. The `private` flag is unchanged.\n3. template-shell/package.json: esbuild''s `peerDependenciesMeta.optional`\n   flipped to `false` - it stays a devDependency, but build/mf-gts.ts\n   imports it unconditionally, so a consumer of that export must not be\n   able to skip installing it.\n4. .github/CODEOWNERS: restored a catch-all `* @GeraBart` above the\n   existing template/scripts/.github entries (he is the architect and owns\n   template and CLI design), and corrected the header''s \"no reason to\n   review\" framing.\n5. main.yml''s `validate` job matrix now runs `[24.14.x, 25.x]`, matching\n   package.json''s `engines` floor (`>=24.14.0`, engine-strict) and\n   gears-frontx''s own matrix - it previously ran 25.x only.\n6. Stale text swept while the split is fresh: template-discovery.mjs''s\n   MANIFEST_FILENAME docblock no longer points at a sync-guard test that\n   was already dropped; the `@param rootDir monorepo root` docblocks across\n   version-bump-on-change-check.mjs, template-ecosystem-packages.mjs, and\n   template-pin-drift-check.mjs now say what `rootDir` actually means today\n   (this repo''s root, or the sibling ecosystem checkout where applicable);\n   link-template-ecosystem.mjs''s header no longer says \"in-monorepo\".\n\nPlus two smaller items flagged alongside: .gitignore restores\n`*.tsbuildinfo` and `coverage/` (template-shell''s `composite: true` and\ncoverage output need both, and its own .gitignore covers neither); and\ntemplate-shell/package.json now declares `jsdom` as a devDependency\n(src-app/vitest.config.ts''s `environment: ''jsdom''` previously resolved only\nvia hoisting from packages/react and packages/studio).\n\nVerified standalone and composed: root `npm ci && npm test` (267/267) and\nall seven root policy scripts (validate:templates, policy:template-pin-\ndrift, policy:template-lockfile-selflink, policy:token-format, policy:\nguideline-index, policy:template-mfes-import-boundary, policy:version-bump-\non-change against origin/main) pass. template-shell/: npm ci, build,\ntype-check, lint, arch:deps, and test:unit all pass standalone. The\ncomposed shell+overlay check main.yml''s template-validate job runs was\nreproduced by hand (template-mfe''s four fixture MFEs overlaid onto a\ntemplate-shell copy): install, build, type-check, arch:deps, lint, and\ntest:unit all pass - this also confirmed that the `npm ls`-visible \"invalid\"\nalias on the root''s `file:.` self-link override is a display artifact of\nnpm < 11.13.0 (the sandbox''s original npm 11.7.0 could not resolve the\ncomposed tree''s exact-pinned `@gears-frontx/frontx-template-shell`\ndependency at all; npm 11.14.0, past CONTRIBUTING.md''s documented npm/cli#524\nfix threshold, resolves and builds it cleanly - not a regression from this\nre-sync).\n\nInvestigated gears-frontx''s own `publish-template` job failure on e4351bc3\nat \"Install + build template\": it is a real, but unrelated and\nalready-obsolete, lockfile desync in that source commit itself (`npm ci`\nthere rejects because template-shell/package-lock.json still pinned\ngts-plugin@0.3.0-alpha.4 against a package.json bumped to 0.3.0-alpha.6),\nnot a pin-not-yet-published race and not something this re-sync could\ninherit, since gears-frontx#615 has since removed the template tree from\nthat repo entirely.\n\n## QA follow-up: dead publish-sort entry, PR-body correction, jsdom regression fix\n\nThree items raised in QA review of the re-sync commit, folded in here:\n\n- `.github/workflows/publish-packages.yml`''s dependency-order sort ranked\n  `@gears-frontx/frontx-template-shell` alongside the leaf packages with a\n  \"the template lib first\" comment - dead code, since `detect-template`''s\n  own `IS_PRIVATE` filter already drops the private `template-shell` root\n  before `PACKAGES` is built, so that name can never reach the sort. Removed\n  the rank entry and the comment.\n- Corrected an inaccurate PR-body claim: the `npm ls` \"invalid\" alias on the\n  root''s `file:.` self-link override (under `packages/framework`) is not\n  gated on npm/cli#524''s 11.13.0 fix threshold - it reproduces on every npm\n  version tested, 11.7.0 through 11.14.0. It is cosmetic, inherent to a\n  package overriding its own name to `file:.` while also being resolved as\n  an ordinary versioned dependency elsewhere in the graph; the symlink it\n  describes resolves correctly regardless.\n- Found and fixed a real, deterministic (not flaky) regression QA''s own\n  verification pass surfaced: `packages/studio`''s `ThemeSelector.test.tsx`\n  hangs opening its Radix dropdown via `userEvent.click` under jsdom,\n  timing out at 30s in the \"portals the open menu...\" case and running\n  suspiciously long (20s+) in the sibling case that also opens the menu.\n  `fireEvent.click` (144ms) versus `userEvent.click` (hangs) isolated the\n  hang to user-event''s own `getComputedStyle`-based pointer-events check,\n  not Radix or `@gears-frontx/ui-kit` (`packages/studio`''s dropdown/button\n  are local, Radix-based components under `src/uikit/`; ui-kit''s\n  0.4.0-alpha.3 changes are confined to `packages/ui-kit/src/styles/\n  theme.css` token values and never reach this code path - confirmed\n  against the published alpha.2/alpha.3 dist and against gears-frontx''s own\n  history, which shows zero commits under `template-shell/packages/studio`\n  in the 1531fba3..e4351bc3 range). Bisecting the lockfile-wide dependency\n  deltas by override found the cause: jsdom''s transitive `nwsapi` (its CSS\n  selector-matching engine) resolved to 2.2.27 here versus 2.2.24\n  previously. 2.2.24 and 2.2.25 are fast; 2.2.26 and 2.2.27 both reproduce\n  the 20-40s hang, consistent with `getComputedStyle` walking\n  `packages/studio`''s Tailwind-style escaped `STUDIO_CSS` attribute\n  selectors during every click. Pinned `\"nwsapi\": \"2.2.24\"` via `overrides`\n  in both `template-shell/package.json` and `template-mfe/package.json`\n  (documented in each manifest''s own `\"//\"` field, cross-referenced between\n  the two) - neither template imports `nwsapi` directly; both reach it only\n  through their shared `jsdom` devDependency. Regenerated both lockfiles.\n\nVerified: root policy scripts and `npm test` (267/267) unaffected;\n`packages/studio`''s standalone suite (26/26) and the composed shell+overlay\nrun of it both pass in under 3 seconds, six consecutive runs each with no\nfailures - versus the 100%-reproducible hang before the pin.\n\n## QA follow-up 2: the composition step''s self-link ETARGET\n\nFork CI on `01f16a79` still failed `template-validate`''s \"Validate shell +\noverlay composition\" step: `npm install` there (main.yml''s step reconciles\nthe shell''s committed lockfile against the newly-overlaid `template-mfe`\nworkspace members) errored `ETARGET No matching version found for\n@gears-frontx/frontx-template-shell@0.1.0-alpha.4` - none of the four\n`template-mfe` fixtures'' exact pins on the shell''s own package resolved\nthrough its `\"@gears-frontx/frontx-template-shell\": \"file:.\"` override.\n\nRoot cause, confirmed by bisecting npm versions against both a from-scratch\n`npm install` and an incremental one: no currently released npm reconciles\n`template-shell/package-lock.json`''s single self-link entry\n(`node_modules/@gears-frontx/frontx-template-shell`) correctly once\nanything else in the tree changes.\n- A from-scratch install/`npm ci` regeneration (tried on 11.7.0, 11.12.1 and\n  11.14.0 - the runner''s own npm is 11.12.1, confirmed via the failing job''s\n  own \"Environment details\" log) mis-writes the entry to resolve through\n  `packages/framework` instead of the root itself - cosmetically an\n  \"invalid\" alias under `npm ls`, but load-bearing wrong: a sibling\n  workspace member''s plain-semver pin on the root''s own name can no longer\n  resolve through it, which is exactly what the composition step''s\n  freshly-added `template-mfe` fixtures need.\n- An incremental `npm install` on top of the *previously correct* lockfile\n  (edit `package.json`, keep `node_modules`) is worse: it drops the entry\n  from the installed tree entirely, matching npm/cli#524''s description in\n  CONTRIBUTING.md to the letter.\n\nOnly the entry as originally committed at `929fe9b5`\n(`{ \"resolved\": \"\", \"link\": true }`) is correct, and no install operation\navailable today can re-derive it - it can only be preserved. Fixed by\nregenerating `template-shell/package-lock.json` (and confirming\n`template-mfe/package-lock.json`, which links to `template-shell` by\nsibling path rather than self-reference, was never affected and needed no\nchange), then restoring that one entry''s value by hand before committing.\n`policy:template-lockfile-selflink` still passes, because it only reads the\nentry - the check never needed npm to have written it correctly in the\nfirst place.\n\nDocumented the failure mode and the by-hand fix in CONTRIBUTING.md''s\nlockfile note, next to the existing npm/cli#524 paragraph it extends.\n\nVerified end to end, twice - once with npm 11.12.1 (the runner''s own\nversion, per the failing job''s log) and once with npm 10.9.4 (this repo''s\n`packageManager`): `template-shell/`''s own `npm ci`, `build`, `type-check`,\n`lint`, `arch:deps`, `test:unit` (all packages, `packages/studio` 26/26);\nand the composed shell+overlay reproduction of `main.yml`''s\n\"Validate shell + overlay composition\" step exactly - overlay `template-mfe`\nonto a copy of `template-shell` outside the repo, `npm install` (not `ci`,\nmatching the workflow), `FRONTX_INCLUDE_TEMPLATE_EXAMPLES=1 npm run build`,\n`FRONTX_INCLUDE_TEMPLATE_EXAMPLES=1 npm run type-check`, `npm run arch:deps`,\n`npm run lint`, `npm run test:unit` - all green under both npm versions,\nwhere every one of these failed with the prior lockfile under 11.12.1.\n`npm run policy:template-lockfile-selflink` passes at the root under both\nversions as well.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Vuk D. <davydowiktor@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"06846533c5da28f1542d08da43692a1832307f7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/git/trees/06846533c5da28f1542d08da43692a1832307f7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/gears-frontx-templates/git/commits/65685ae749f503965b7d0aa6a22498fd1da48f4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_a