\n- CG-3: generator produces the local override manifest\n- TSB-1: shell has no baked-in fallback remotes\n\nAlso updates CONTEXT.md glossary with:\n- Demo tier clarification (per-customer demo deployments)\n- Local vs dev environment distinction","tree":{"sha":"9cd04eaf53b2566c8ae9f8a36705873da070a810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/trees/9cd04eaf53b2566c8ae9f8a36705873da070a810"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/commits/697524f6e42a6f0dbff557e6e8d945f05ef14e0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cd04eaf53b2566c8ae9f8a36705873da070a810\nparent 4a509ed1710a580e78c4bac245e385c5340adc23\nauthor alirazatss <158475089+alirazatss@users.noreply.github.com> 1786717517 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786717517 +0200\n\ndocs(spec): add remote-config-environment-cleanup OpenSpec change (#91)\n\nAdd OpenSpec change for remote config environment cleanup with four task groups:\n1. Shell env config relocation & local override serving\n2. Config generator: local mode, root MFE, local override output\n3. Remove baked-in fallback remotes (fail visible)\n4. ADRs and glossary consistency\n\nRequirements covered:\n- ESRC-1: env config files live in config/, none under public/\n- ESRC-2: build emits exactly one manifest selected by DEPLOY_ENV\n- ESRC-3: dev server serves gitignored local override with dev-config fallback\n- CG-1: environment mode ''local'' replaces ''development''\n- CG-2: generator honors shell''s root MFE designation\n- CG-3: generator produces the local override manifest\n- TSB-1: shell has no baked-in fallback remotes\n\nAlso updates CONTEXT.md glossary with:\n- Demo tier clarification (per-customer demo deployments)\n- Local vs dev environment distinction","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfyVNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACQIQAJekKxTA7ayApP48fJOLGT3s\nyt5eWvGHvLWg+p1giFaPmHpwgczeg+zbVNcumGcUQy17s/95PDdFipnowq2V+GtS\nbbuhtvIbN3g+kP31bCouCrR0S1PUsVFBSVkPCMvULMZIZ