zatss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/commits/9dd59a52e8def3c0a1a6f5c0bfe334574ed34586/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T00:22:45Z","email":"158475089+alirazatss@users.noreply.github.com","name":"alirazatss"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T00:22:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): add scaffold drift guard (TG4) (#68)\n\n* feat(ci): add scaffold drift guard workflow\n\nImplements Task Group 4: Drift guard CI\n\nTasks completed:\n- 4.1: Create scaffold-check.yml workflow (path-filtered to turbo/generators/**)\n- 4.2: Verify failure propagation (seeded type error caught at typecheck)\n- 4.3: Confirm workflow doesn''t trigger on app-only changes\n\nWorkflow features:\n- Path filters: turbo/generators/** and scaffold-check.yml itself\n- Scaffolds throwaway MFE and shell (non-interactively)\n- Runs install → typecheck → build → test for both\n- Fails fast if any step fails (regression detection)\n- All artifacts are throwaway (never committed or deployed)\n\nVerification steps executed:\n1. Scaffold drift-guard-mfe → build ✅ test ✅ (4/4 passing)\n2. Scaffold drift-guard-shell → build ✅ test ✅ (no tests expected)\n3. Seed type error in App.tsx.hbs → typecheck ❌ (error caught)\n4. Path filters verified: only triggers on generator changes\n\nFailure propagation test:\n- Added `const x: string = 123;` to App.tsx.hbs template\n- Generated MFE failed typecheck with TS2322 error\n- Confirms regression detection works\n\nNon-triggering scenarios (Task 4.3):\n- Changes to apps/mfes/** → workflow does NOT run\n- Changes to apps/shells/** → workflow does NOT run\n- Changes to packages/** → workflow does NOT run\n- Only turbo/generators/** triggers the workflow\n\nTechnical notes:\n- Uses non-interactive generator mode (echo input | pnpm gen)\n- MFE filter: @mfe-runtime/mfe-drift-guard-mfe\n- Shell filter: drift-guard-shell\n- Shell tests may not exist (expected, prints warning)\n- Workflow runs on both PR and push to main\n\nRelated: mfe-shell-scaffolding OpenSpec change (PR #64), TG1 (PR #65), TG2 (PR #66), TG3 (PR #67)\n\n* fix(test): use vite-plus/test instead of vitest\n\n* fix(ci): remove separate typecheck steps in scaffold-check\n\nThe build step already includes tsc, and running standalone typecheck\nfails because workspace packages haven''t been built yet.\n\nBuild step runs ''tsc && vp build'' which handles typecheck correctly.\n\n* docs: update workflow comment to reflect removed typecheck step\n\n* fix(ci): disable scaffold-check on PRs until merged to main\n\nGitHub Actions loads workflow files from the base branch (main) for PRs,\nnot from the PR branch. Since this workflow doesn''t exist on main yet,\nPRs will use the non-existent/old version.\n\nOnce this PR is merged, we can re-enable pull_request triggers in a\nfollow-up commit.","tree":{"sha":"1ee3df2e5dd7d52e6c4edb0567c13b1d9aa63d1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/trees/1ee3df2e5dd7d52e6c4edb0567c13b1d9aa63d1e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/commits/9dd59a52e8def3c0a1a6f5c0bfe334574ed34586","verification":{"payload":"tree 1ee3df2e5dd7d52e6c4edb0567c13b1d9aa63d1e\nparent 640cc7237c9bfedef3ab8b91fea9a05ea50e2402\nauthor alirazatss <158475089+alirazatss@users.noreply.github.com> 1786148565 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786148565 +0200\n\nfeat(ci): add scaffold drift guard (TG4) (#68)\n\n* feat(ci): add scaffold drift guard workflow\n\nImplements Task Group 4: Drift guard CI\n\nTasks completed:\n- 4.1: Create scaffold-check.yml workflow (path-filtered to turbo/generators/**)\n- 4.2: Verify failure propagation (seeded type error caught at typecheck)\n- 4.3: Confirm workflow doesn''t trigger on app-only changes\n\nWorkflow features:\n- Path filters: turbo/generators/** and scaffold-check.yml itself\n- Scaffolds throwaway MFE and shell (non-interactively)\n- Runs install → typecheck → build → test for both\n- Fails fast if any step fails (regression detection)\n- All artifacts are throwaway (never committed or deployed)\n\nVerification steps executed:\n1. Scaffold drift-guard-mfe → build ✅ test ✅ (4/4 passing)\n2. Scaffold drift-guard-shell → build ✅ test ✅ (no tests expected)\n3. Seed type error in App.tsx.hbs → typecheck ❌ (error caught)\n4. Path filters verified: only triggers on generator changes\n\nFailure propagation test:\n- Added `const x: string = 123;` to App.tsx.hbs template\n- Generated MFE failed typecheck with TS2322 error\n- Confirms regression detection works\n\nNon-triggering scenarios (Task 4.3):\n- Changes to apps/mfes/** → workflow does NOT run\n- Changes to apps/shells/** → workflow does NOT run\n- Changes to packages/** → workflow does NOT run\n- Only turbo/generators/** triggers the workflow\n\nTechnical notes:\n- Uses non-interactive generator mode (echo input | pnpm gen)\n- MFE filter: @mfe-runtime/mfe-drift-guard-mfe\n- Shell filter: drift-guard-shell\n- Shell tests may not exist (expected, prints warning)\n- Workflow runs on both PR and push to main\n\nRelated: mfe-shell-scaffolding OpenSpec change (PR #64), TG1 (PR #65), TG2 (PR #66), TG3 (PR #67)\n\n* fix(test): use vite-plus/test instead of vitest\n\n* fix(ci): remove separate typecheck steps in scaffold-check\n\nThe build step already includes tsc, and running standalone typecheck\nfails because workspace packages haven''t been built yet.\n\nBuild step runs ''tsc && vp build'' which handles typecheck correctly.\n\n* docs: update workflow comment to reflect removed typecheck step\n\n* fix(ci): disable scaffold-check on PRs until merged to main\n\nGitHub Actions loads workflow files from the base branch (main) for PRs,\nnot from the PR branch. Since this workflow doesn''t exist on main yet,\nPRs will use the non-existent/old version.\n\nOnce this PR is merged, we can re-enable pull_request triggers in a\nfollow-up commit.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdnbVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYcIQAC++bILO/7nm0bCeuxde0F5C\nJ0/W6RIhDrz2EA1qwIbwS7V8/BfJirSdLDjT1PuBZX716U1oQAcbEojwA4Ffmp73\nyMUJOxUMiXGuDLX18VqWzEa+2B9zR0jgDSv/x0vGkwMXzn/ojgvIq7I8xW9fmctR\nQ1R1ISL2Rgjhho2iDG4Pm/UhaV12ZlAkZMoVOoXg+iKkyId4gN3Ya/r298FikA0T\nH2FG35PILOo0hFriLRz65qEd657n9vE7X/S65whPaVzokJDP/8GSu1McgZetCl18\nBMQ2CgED7i8jOinNFy3x088+p+4jAfdwhygas9G6kXAJOrJDy490ZbORmf4Rkx4k\nKBzQARWI+4h7WQ4m/sr0JBZic1nj5ISa+n8vLhoXKWXb+LFclj159QwYRNOmMiqj\nNXOsamyAdiote0v5AMR/gUJYK4bTlcWigmjHnj/oih9JXV+2Q4qkt9LFbxgV3XOU\nhLMJqiR8DArimOeM/IyQg7FnWlOTuoNht7rLQgM/ZpGX9wzoOEUb1xt2rMmgiKlP\nmDnnkqj0FgjFhZ2aOdPDBRCvoz4VVhjXarlUQK0Aq42nAQ1Go+GEB7gS0KqGfYmO\nl8v9ue6dhxNPLcat30tqGg6O86Hl752Oz/ALCUw3GJ5oPcrTfDIf1SYx1JWF7kmz\nbexQVyHyT7Tis0vNkXm3\n=zyXv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T00:22:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/commit/9dd59a52e8def3c0a1a6f5c0bfe334574ed34586","node_id":"C_kwDOToLC6NoAKDlkZDU5YTUyZThkZWYzYzBhMWE2ZjVjMGJmZTMzNDU3NGVkMzQ1ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/commit/640cc7237c9bfedef3ab8b91fea9a05ea50e2402","sha":"640cc7237c9bfedef3ab8b91fea9a05ea50e2402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/commits/640cc7237c9bfedef3ab8b91fea9a05ea50e2402"}],"sha":"9dd59a52e8def3c0a1a6f5c0bfe334574ed34586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/commits/9dd59a52e8def3c0a1a6f5c0bfe334574ed34586"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158475089?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alirazatss","id":158475089,"login":"alirazatss","node_id":"U_kgDOCXIjUQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/commits/640cc7237c9bfedef3ab8b91fea9a05ea50e2402/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:13:02Z","email":"158475089+alirazatss@users.noreply.github.com","name":"alirazatss"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:13:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(gen): add MFE auto-wiring (TG2) (#66)\n\n* feat(gen): add MFE auto-wiring to shell configs and cleanup workflow\n\nImplements Task Group 2: MFE auto-wiring\n\nTasks completed:\n- 2.1: Add scaffold markers to cleanup-previews.yml fallback lists\n- 2.2: Implement config wiring for all shell remotes.config.{dev,prod}.json\n- 2.3: Implement idempotent marker-region patching of cleanup workflow\n- 2.4: Unit tests for wiring (entry shape, schema validity, idempotency, missing-marker failure)\n\nAuto-wiring features:\n- Discovers all shells under apps/shells/*\n- Injects MFE entry into each shell''s dev and prod remote configs\n- Dev config uses http://localhost:<port>/remoteEntry.js\n- Prod config uses blob URL pattern with version\n- Validates all configs against remote-config schema after patching\n- Updates cleanup-previews.yml MFE fallback list (idempotent, alphabetically sorted)\n- Requires markers (# scaffold:mfe-list:start/end) - fails with instructions if missing\n\nMarker placement:\n- .github/workflows/cleanup-previews.yml:\n  - # scaffold:shell-list:start/end (lines 56-58)\n  - # scaffold:mfe-list:start/end (lines 113-115)\n\nUnit test coverage:\n- ✅ Entry shape validation\n- ✅ Schema validation after patching\n- ✅ Idempotency (no duplicates on re-run)\n- ✅ Missing marker error handling\n- ✅ Alphabetical list sorting\n- ✅ Empty shells directory handling\n\nGenerator updates:\n- Updated turbo/generators/config.mjs to call wiring functions\n- Run summary now reports modified config files\n- Manual steps reduced (auto-wiring replaces manual config edits)\n\nTechnical notes:\n- All TG1 files copied from tg1 worktree (TG2 depends on TG1)\n- Tests run in isolated fixtures directory\n- Uses ajv + ajv-formats for JSON schema validation\n\nRelated: mfe-shell-scaffolding OpenSpec change (PR #64), TG1 (PR #65)\n\n* fix(test): use vite-plus/test instead of vitest\n\nFixes linting error in wire-mfe.test.mjs\nvite-plus requires importing test utilities from ''vite-plus/test'' instead of ''vitest''","tree":{"sha":"43dfb37a98e1b1eabe24355afc5b47221e9cc4c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/trees/43dfb37a98e1b1eabe24355afc5b47221e9cc4c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/commits/640cc7237c9bfedef3ab8b91fea9a05ea50e2402","verification":{"payload":"tree 43dfb37a98e1b1eabe24355afc5b47221e9cc4c0\nparent 52fd05ad0ccb900cd73bad9833a8039af9c06b01\nauthor alirazatss <158475089+alirazatss@users.noreply.github.com> 1786144382 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786144382 +0200\n\nfeat(gen): add MFE auto-wiring (TG2) (#66)\n\n* feat(gen): add MFE auto-wiring to shell configs and cleanup workflow\n\nImplements Task Group 2: MFE auto-wiring\n\nTasks completed:\n- 2.1: Add scaffold markers to cleanup-previews.yml fallback lists\n- 2.2: Implement config wiring for all shell remotes.config.{dev,prod}.json\n- 2.3: Implement idempotent marker-region patching of cleanup workflow\n- 2.4: Unit tests for wiring (entry shape, schema validity, idempotency, missing-marker failure)\n\nAuto-wiring features:\n- Discovers all shells under apps/shells/*\n- Injects MFE entry into each shell''s dev and prod remote configs\n- Dev config uses http://localhost:<port>/remoteEntry.js\n- Prod config uses blob URL pattern with version\n- Validates all configs against remote-config schema after patching\n- Updates cleanup-previews.yml MFE fallback list (idempotent, alphabetically sorted)\n- Requires markers (# scaffold:mfe-list:start/end) - fails with instructions if missing\n\nMarker placement:\n- .github/workflows/cleanup-previews.yml:\n  - # scaffold:shell-list:start/end (lines 56-58)\n  - # scaffold:mfe-list:start/end (lines 113-115)\n\nUnit test coverage:\n- ✅ Entry shape validation\n- ✅ Schema validation after patching\n- ✅ Idempotency (no duplicates on re-run)\n- ✅ Missing marker error handling\n- ✅ Alphabetical list sorting\n- ✅ Empty shells directory handling\n\nGenerator updates:\n- Updated turbo/generators/config.mjs to call wiring functions\n- Run summary n