tarred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alirazatss","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/commits/dc1acf840d08674884a1fdbfe2d97e2a1bc3f8ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T22:27:36Z","email":"158475089+alirazatss@users.noreply.github.com","name":"alirazatss"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T22:27:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): portable validator CLI (tasks 3.1-3.5) [app-config-contract] (#43)\n\n* feat(ci): implement task group 3 (portable validator CLI) [app-config-contract]\n\nImplements tasks 3.1–3.5 from openspec/changes/app-config-contract/tasks.md.\n\nRequirements covered:\n- AVT-1: Portable validator with file + URL support\n- AVT-2: CI validation of public config\n- AAR-3: Schema drift detection\n\nCreated portable validator CLI with:\n- scripts/validate-app-config.ts: ajv-based validator\n- Accepts schema and document as file paths or HTTP(S) URLs\n- Zero imports from shell/app internals (fully portable)\n- Exit codes: 0 (valid), 1 (invalid), 2 (error)\n- Comprehensive test suite (8 tests, all passing)\n\nCI Integration:\n- New ''validate-app-config'' job in test.yml\n- Schema drift check: regenerates and compares to committed version\n- Validates apps/shells/website/public/app-config.json\n- Added to CI gate (blocking)\n\nTests: 8 passing (+ 1 skipped URL test)\n- Valid/invalid document scenarios\n- Exit code verification\n- Error handling (file not found, HTTP errors)\n- Real schema validation\n\nVerification evidence in PR description.\n\n* fix(ci): format schema after generation in drift check\n\nThe drift check needs to format the schema after generation to match\nthe committed version (which was formatted by vp check --fix).\n\nUpdated instructions to include formatting step.\n\n* fix(ci): use pnpm exec vp for schema formatting\n\nvp is not in PATH in CI environment, need to use pnpm exec vp.","tree":{"sha":"f2f6d9ad71e4e646bb9fc93106e23e34d9e149d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/trees/f2f6d9ad71e4e646bb9fc93106e23e34d9e149d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alirazatss/mfe-catalog/git/commits/dc1acf840d08674884a1fdbfe2d97e2a1bc3f8ad","verification":{"payload":"tree f2f6d9ad71e4e646bb9fc93106e23e34d9e149d5\nparent c8255e61ba79621b8349de6c7672c22a491c2bec\nauthor alirazatss <158475089+alirazatss@users.noreply.github.com> 1785968856 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785968856 +0200\n\nfeat(ci): portable validator CLI (tasks 3.1-3.5) [app-config-contract] (#43)\n\n* feat(ci): implement task group 3 (portable validator CLI) [app-config-contract]\n\nImplements tasks 3.1–3.5 from openspec/changes/app-config-contract/tasks.md.\n\nRequirements covered:\n- AVT-1: Portable validator with file + URL support\n- AVT-2: CI validation of public config\n- AAR-3: Schema drift detection\n\nCreated portable validator CLI with:\n- scripts/validate-app-config.ts: ajv-based validator\n- Accepts schema and document as file paths or HTTP(S) URLs\n- Zero imports from shell/app internals (fully portable)\n- Exit codes: 0 (valid), 1 (invalid), 2 (error)\n- Comprehensive test suite (8 tests, all passing)\n\nCI Integration:\n- New ''validate-app-config'' job in test.yml\n- Schema drift check: regenerates and compares to committed version\n- Validates apps/shells/website/public/app-config.json\n- Added to CI gate (blocking)\n\nTests: 8 passing (+ 1 skipped URL test)\n- Valid/invalid document scenarios\n- Exit code verification\n- Error handling (file not found, HTTP errors)\n- Real schema validation\n\nVerification evidence in PR description.\n\n* fix(ci): format schema after generation in drift check\n\nThe drift check needs to format the schema after generation to match\nthe committed version (which was formatted by vp check --fix).\n\nUpdated instructions to include formatting step.\n\n* fix(ci): use pnpm exec vp for schema formatting\n\nvp is not in PATH in CI environment, need to use pnpm exec vp.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc7jYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvxMQAG65n3VvXtw7Bu9JDkiG2Xvu\nlL/byHnV5f4EI8gWbpHn7WN2bpzPOy7CyMVF7gNliVpfeiVhWCvQ3UxathLtUqSu\n6oZeRMThxJn//3ORmxlNsoOeHWuIYIx+5LL+vMD1278r2m7yFeJpt1/a9VtHbpNm\nJKJn8kTcPlH/xvyB4UFhsqzYoCKAA2oexjRmfwlIsLxZ9e+lWTpzgblWL5xwYYoA\nu82YjQufvqiKYTciy9a327LvxO83WSVNcT1tqQ0LSww0YA3xs2wu2zLTIvVmosOu\nKizMwJ5Ybtsde51XHFYVhakwV2LUwtlX/VnxeB+aym8D7ZNF2dZL23+ABALCqQpQ\n6ysbf8mZxAMI9pYfbROCv5+XzRH6RpRZW89hD+C+MMQRJYKMNZJaMp4aTRwoGzTA\nsn4TfZrp2R9iXItJ8CjklWa9cyznvNNY2fXOilqmgxLvarKYIhkwA/HHmMIqarQb\nMYITpWtwI1sVLi8nWYGHwPFUy58N1d5xnduPAsIWYf3P+yil+ofY8pjgg9T+viIQ\njb1BLwioMvwY28IrRiw2+hrHzgwfFBo2d5KaE55jETsMxEramYT97nBcOlOWngTU\nscmCBhIpMQQ6bSWUxE0zUEPKKl/eYuBNy5nAnajtDULYzfrrUbIhb4nujGfMQM+i\nUvnFGcCBPJYeieU/oSdc\n=ke5a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T00:05:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"