ps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ASKO647/glop-ai/commit/9913de973cce97cb222b812dab603fa3df2c3501","node_id":"C_kwDOToj_ZdoAKDk5MTNkZTk3M2NjZTk3Y2IyMjJiODEyZGFiNjAzZmEzZGYyYzM1MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ASKO647/glop-ai/commit/51377b512fae157d0063625d41d3fa924691de09","sha":"51377b512fae157d0063625d41d3fa924691de09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ASKO647/glop-ai/commits/51377b512fae157d0063625d41d3fa924691de09"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ASKO647/glop-ai/commit/c7eb04a0ba1cffc9d2e663588ad6941e11ae9e7e","sha":"c7eb04a0ba1cffc9d2e663588ad6941e11ae9e7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ASKO647/glop-ai/commits/c7eb04a0ba1cffc9d2e663588ad6941e11ae9e7e"}],"sha":"9913de973cce97cb222b812dab603fa3df2c3501","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ASKO647/glop-ai/commits/9913de973cce97cb222b812dab603fa3df2c3501"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ASKO647/glop-ai/commits/c7eb04a0ba1cffc9d2e663588ad6941e11ae9e7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T18:39:14Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T18:39:14Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix avatar re-upload, rework progress photos into 3 slots, add AI analysis\n\n- Fix profile photo appearing stuck after a replacement: the storage\n  path is always {user_id}/avatar.jpg, so avatarPath never actually\n  changes on re-upload and the sign() effect never reran. useAvatar\n  now force-resigns after a successful upload and appends a\n  cache-busting &t= timestamp to the signed URL so RN''s <Image>\n  treats it as a new resource.\n- Replace unlimited daily progress photos with exactly three fixed\n  slots (avant/milieu/apres). hooks/useProgressPhotos.ts is keyed by\n  slot instead of date, storage path is {user_id}/{slot}.jpg, and\n  carries the same cache-busting fix as the avatar (fixed path per\n  slot has the same staleness risk). PhotosCard.tsx now renders three\n  3:4 frames with slot labels, a dashed empty state with an \"Ajouter\"\n  prompt, and a date/weight overlay on filled frames; tapping any\n  frame (empty or filled) opens the picker and replaces that slot,\n  long-press on a filled frame offers deletion.\n- Add lib/progressAnalysis.ts: sends the available progress photos\n  (each preceded by a text block naming its slot and date) plus the\n  user''s goal/weights to Claude, asking for a strict JSON comparison\n  (resume, points_positifs, axes_travail, score). The system prompt\n  restricts the model to visible physical changes only, forbids\n  devaluing commentary and medical advice. Photos are fetched from\n  their signed URL and base64-encoded on the fly, since they may have\n  been uploaded in an earlier session rather than being a fresh local\n  URI. components/progression/ScoreRing.tsx + ProgressAnalysisCard.tsx\n  render the result (score ring, summary, bulleted lists) under an\n  \"Analyser ma progression\" / \"Réanalyser\" button, enabled once at\n  least two slots are filled.\n- Move stripJsonFences into lib/anthropic.ts (now shared between\n  foodScanner and progressAnalysis) instead of duplicating it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LvCRYw2iKcBLvspwPHJ5Li","tree":{"sha":"cb757616826533ca258af71cfee6eacbece1b337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ASKO647/glop-ai/git/trees/cb757616826533ca258af71cfee6eacbece1b337"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ASKO647/glop-ai/git/commits/c7eb04a0ba1cffc9d2e663588ad6941e11ae9e7e","verification":{"payload":"tree cb757616826533ca258af71cfee6eacbece1b337\nparent ca225b82b9b406954ae58a643c1c0a982a1bcb9d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785609554 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785609554 +0000\n\nFix avatar re-upload, rework progress photos into 3 slots, add AI analysis\n\n- Fix profile photo appearing stuck after a replacement: the storage\n  path is always {user_id}/avatar.jpg, so avatarPath never actually\n  changes on re-upload and the sign() effect never reran. useAvatar\n  now force-resigns after a successful upload and appends a\n  cache-busting &t= timestamp to the signed URL so RN''s <Image>\n  treats it as a new resource.\n- Replace unlimited daily progress photos with exactly three fixed\n  slots (avant/milieu/apres). hooks/useProgressPhotos.ts is keyed by\n  slot instead of date, storage path is {user_id}/{slot}.jpg, and\n  carries the same cache-busting fix as the avatar (fixed path per\n  slot has the same staleness risk). PhotosCard.tsx now renders three\n  3:4 frames with slot labels, a dashed empty state with an \"Ajouter\"\n  prompt, and a date/weight overlay on filled frames; tapping any\n  frame (empty or filled) opens the picker and replaces that slot,\n  long-press on a filled frame offers deletion.\n- Add lib/progressAnalysis.ts: sends the available progress photos\n  (each preceded by a text block naming its slot and date) plus the\n  user''s goal/weights to Claude, asking for a strict JSON comparison\n  (resume, points_positifs, axes_travail, score). The system prompt\n  restricts the model to visible physical changes only, forbids\n  devaluing commentary and medical advice. Photos are fetched from\n  their signed URL and base64-encoded on the fly, since they may have\n  been uploaded in an earlier session rather than being a fresh local\n  URI. components/progression/ScoreRing.tsx + ProgressAnalysisCard.tsx\n  render the result (score ring, summary, bulleted lists) under an\n  \"Analyser ma progression\" / \"Réanalyser\" button, enabled once at\n  least two slots are filled.\n- Move stripJsonFences into lib/anthropic.ts (now shared between\n  foodScanner and progressAnalysis) instead of duplicating it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LvCRYw2iKcBLvspwPHJ5Li\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIOoawio\nlaVeEgyS137GouBUyWnbAXf/LCZhvMnmpXkvxioQl1/uEkmKeP9297fNQ7yXqFqlAYDPuZlNrn6o\nRgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:39:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node