e25e33d5f65739d76d58960012e3c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9914ca842204f7fcc990203239113920d5b2b7d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T21:14:06Z","email":"savvanisspiros@gmail.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T21:14:06Z","email":"savvanisspiros@gmail.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"Re-render, and pick up a testnet tree four releases behind\n\nThe mainnet half is the change this branch made: `secret-outbox` on the `pool`\nDeployment and its migrate Job, and nothing else. Two envFrom blocks, exactly\nwhat adding one `env_file:` to a compose service is supposed to produce.\n\nThe testnet half is drift the render exposed rather than caused. Its four files\nwere last generated at 2026.8.108 while mainnet moved on to 2026.8.114, so the\ntree carried a stale release stamp and four stale per-release Job names. No\nworkload changed; a `git diff` of that half is stamps and names alone. It is\nincluded rather than left because a partial render is exactly the state\n`check-k8s-render-matches-compose.py` exists to refuse — its own header says a\ndirectory whose four files name different releases is a shape it has to catch,\nand leaving one half at an older release would have kept that true after this\nmerge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"2b85a4a8bced1444f59fe9445d31772a67805bbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/2b85a4a8bced1444f59fe9445d31772a67805bbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/9914ca842204f7fcc990203239113920d5b2b7d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/9914ca842204f7fcc990203239113920d5b2b7d4","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDk5MTRjYTg0MjIwNGY3ZmNjOTkwMjAzMjM5MTEzOTIwZDViMmI3ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e","sha":"25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e"}],"sha":"9914ca842204f7fcc990203239113920d5b2b7d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9914ca842204f7fcc990203239113920d5b2b7d4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T21:09:48Z","email":"savvanisspiros@gmail.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T21:09:48Z","email":"savvanisspiros@gmail.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"The four money services join the erasure register, under the owner''s rule\n\n`check-erasure-register.py` has been reporting four failures since it was\nwritten: `wallet`, `ledger`, `custody` and `pool` each store a `user_id` and\nnone of them subscribed to `identity.user.deleted`. They were not an oversight —\nmicro-org#534 held them open on a question no checker could answer for itself:\nwhat does the estate do with a balance, a deposit address, a key and a payout\nowed to a person who has asked to be forgotten?\n\nTHE OWNER ANSWERED IT ON 2026-09-02: **everything is anonymised.** The header of\nthis file now carries the decision in full, including the clause that keeps the\nalready-shipped delete-based handlers legal — deletion stays available where it\nleaves LESS behind than anonymisation would, because it is then the strictly\nstronger form of the same outcome, not a different answer.\n\nThree of the four anonymise and one deletes, and each service''s `erasure.ts`\nargues its own case at length rather than deferring to this table:\n\n  * `ledger` — a journal you can delete a party out of is not a record. Delete an\n    account and every posting referencing it becomes a debit with no counterpart.\n    `accounts.subject` is the only column naming a person, so one UPDATE covers\n    the service, and the test asserts that from `information_schema`.\n\n  * `custody` — the row is half of a key controlling money on a public chain, and\n    the other half is the chain. Deleting it destroys the only route back to an\n    address that still holds coins. The status column is deliberately untouched:\n    `gates.ts` refuses to sign for a non-active key, so retiring a departed\n    person''s deposit address would strand the money rather than the identity.\n\n  * `wallet` — the same argument one level up, plus `idempotency_keys.key`, which\n    is `<userId>:<route>:<clientKey>` and therefore a text PRIMARY KEY carrying\n    the person verbatim. Delivered through agora''s existing webhook as a fan-out\n    sink: `MOUNTED_EVENT_PATHS`''s condition is ONE KEY, NOT THREE, and this module\n    verifies with the same estate-wide secret, so it needs no route, no\n    subscription row and no deploy provisioning of its own.\n\n  * `pool` — DELETES, and the register''s clause is why. `pool_account_links` is\n    the only place a person appears, and anonymising would leave `erased:<uuid> →\n    <account>`: a row whose only content is that somebody who no longer exists\n    mined under that label. Deleting also lands on a path `payouts.ts` already\n    handles — null from `userForAccount` is its NORMAL answer, because most pool\n    accounts are a firmware miner''s own payout address with no estate user at all.\n\nTHE COMPOSE CHANGE IS POOL''S ALONE. It is the one service in the estate that\nread no signing secret, on the recorded ground that it publishes nothing. That\nhalf is still true; what changed is that it now RECEIVES one event, so\n`secrets/outbox.<network>.env` is mounted on both the service and its MIGRATE\nJOB — the migrator imports the same eager `env.ts` and would exit(1) before\ntouching the schema without it. `wallet` needs nothing (agora already has it),\n`ledger` and `custody` already read it to sign their own deliveries.\n\nSeeding is automatic: `estate-bootstrap.sh` already loops this file and\nsubscribes every row, and compares the count rather than printing it.\n\nmicro-org#534. After this, `check-erasure-register.py` reports 24 of 24.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"8adf667cc0666061356050342fc25b30fe21ac08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/8adf667cc0666061356050342fc25b30fe21ac08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDI1ZTBmMTFmZTA4NzRkOThmYmUwNDA2YjFhMDQxYWI5ZGZiOWNkNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/fc96dcf67ce3575da54bd8c3abbd4b6908347022","sha":"fc96dcf67ce3575da54bd8c3abbd4b6908347022","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/fc96dcf67ce3575da54bd8c3abbd4b6908347022"}],"sha":"25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/25e0f11fe0874d98fbe0406b1a041ab9dfb9cd5e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4446752?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/savvaniss/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/savvaniss/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/savvaniss/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github