c0caecb1972b70f3ee30d25b3aa69ce03b595/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:39:10Z","email":"savvanisspiros@gmail.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T06:39:10Z","email":"savvanisspiros@gmail.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"A merge that leaves a file behind leaves a feature behind\n\n`worlds` had a GDPR erasure handler. Written for micro-org#491, reviewed,\nclosed, and corrected as recently as 2026-09-01 — that day''s fix was a leak of\nthe user id into `reward_grants.idempotency_key`, caught by the handler''s own\ncatalogue sweep.\n\nThen commit `078e799` absorbed worlds into agora. It copied TWENTY-SEVEN files\nout of `worlds/src` and copied neither `erasure.ts` nor `erasure.test.ts`.\n\nMeasured on mainnet 2026-09-02, after the subscription was repaired and the 101\nhistorical erasures replayed: 101 deliveries, 0 failures, and **0 inbox rows on\neither plane** — every one taking the `202 {status: ''ignored''}` branch, because\nthe topic dispatch went with the file (micro-org#543).\n\nNothing caught it, and the reason is worth stating plainly:\n`check-erasure-register.py` globs every service''s `src/migrations.ts` under the\nestate root, so it reads the STANDALONE CHECKOUT — which still has the handler,\nbecause absorbing a service does not delete its repository. The register said\nworlds erases. The standalone code did erase. The running module did not. Three\nartefacts, two of them right, and the one that runs was the odd one out.\n\nThis check compares an absorbed module against its own checkout, file by file,\nusing the same two-round absorption discovery `derive-grants.mjs` uses — so\n`hub-api` -> `agora/src/hub` is still found and `looksLikeACopy` still has to\nagree before anything is judged. Four names are allowed to be absent and each\ncarries its reason: `index.ts`, `migrator.ts` and `main.ts` because the absorber\nboots, `module.ts` because the absorber adds it, `kernel.ts` and\n`migratortargets.ts` because `mergedroutes.test.ts` records that widening\ndeliberately. Everything else is a file somebody wrote for that service, and a\nmerge is not the place to decide it is no longer wanted.\n\n`--self-test` builds a fixture with one file left behind, asserts the check\nfails on it, and asserts it passes once the file is restored. It plants nothing\non disk: three of estate-ci''s five canaries planted at a hard-coded path and\naccused the checker the day the layout moved, so this one owns its own tree.\n\nRun against the estate now: 22 absorbed services, all carrying every file — the\none that was not is restored in micro-agora#16.\n\nmicro-org#543.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"33fad664012374c478a672d67d5b303cb91a217a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/33fad664012374c478a672d67d5b303cb91a217a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/de2c0caecb1972b70f3ee30d25b3aa69ce03b595","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/de2c0caecb1972b70f3ee30d25b3aa69ce03b595","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGRlMmMwY2FlY2IxOTcyYjcwZjNlZTMwZDI1YjNhYTY5Y2UwM2I1OTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/56267e8fd9112ed4fc51e8161b6e95e299574915","sha":"56267e8fd9112ed4fc51e8161b6e95e299574915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/56267e8fd9112ed4fc51e8161b6e95e299574915"}],"sha":"de2c0caecb1972b70f3ee30d25b3aa69ce03b595","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/de2c0caecb1972b70f3ee30d25b3aa69ce03b595"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4446752?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/user