t/71aa183ade3202a2e6f061ca5df551963893f2ea","sha":"71aa183ade3202a2e6f061ca5df551963893f2ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/71aa183ade3202a2e6f061ca5df551963893f2ea"}],"sha":"2b800dfb138c0d4b775c571e81c90b128d5cb748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/2b800dfb138c0d4b775c571e81c90b128d5cb748"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/71aa183ade3202a2e6f061ca5df551963893f2ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:40:08Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:40:08Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"conformance runner: mount the trust bundle — I left it out and was wrong\n\nThe argument for omitting it was that every target is a public\n<sub>.cloudsforge.online with a public certificate and beacon is plain HTTP\ninside the cluster, so a CA would widen what this process trusts for nothing.\n\nThe harness refused, and it was right:\n\n  base ''micro'' reaches 10 target(s) over https and NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS is unset,\n  so the estate CA is not trusted and every scenario would skip on a handshake\n  failure that reads like a dead estate.\n\nIt refuses rather than skipping BECAUSE the failure it guards against is\nindistinguishable from a dead estate, and a replay that skipped ten targets\nwould publish, go green and certify nothing. Weakening that check to fit this\ndeployment would be the exact move this estate''s checks exist to prevent.\n\n''s trust.crt is the file for this and says so in its own header:\nthe one passed to  and NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS, one process at a\ntime, never installed anywhere. A ConfigMap and not a Secret, because both roots\nin it are public certificates.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: 