tps://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/aa613beb6293acaa5d8e724ca6bc1b10b55d7eb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:50:52Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:50:52Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"feat(erasure): register worlds, so the event reaches its new handler\n\nmicro-org#491. micro-worlds now has an erasure handler, and without a\nregister row it would never receive the event: identity has ten\nsubscriptions to identity.user.deleted and worlds was not among them, so\nthe handler would have sat there correct and unreachable.\n\nThe row is what both mechanisms read — the deploy seeds the subscription\nfrom it, and erasure-drill.sh takes its coverage from it — so one line\nmakes the handler both reachable and exercised.\n\n`retained` is `-` on purpose. worlds keeps two rows (reward_grants for\nthe ledger link, provisions for the entitlement idempotency) but keeps\nneither IDENTIFIER: both are rewritten to a placeholder, so SCAN must\ncome back clean and a surviving id is a failure rather than a declared\nexception.\n\ncheck-erasure-register.py now reports 18 of 24. The remaining six —\ncustody, foresight, ledger, pool, studio, wallet — are a separate and\nlarger finding than #491 describes; raised there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"284f9aebaa681d79fe8593fea6782bdbff57255d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/284f9aebaa681d79fe8593fea6782bdbff57255d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/aa613beb6293acaa5d8e724ca6bc1b10b55d7eb4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"