4wAyABodm2h5srYZJOEE6azm\nJ8TgEJ9ZEtTsZ3GBQAfkYSU2ybrIsoc+tLnNfmjAsfalBrAFtedW/NXuzo48bBgo\njmAOe5fsGaNfLsKyB95jpAL92ivRs5D2747qfrk0UMczyRFALsX/T0gGXiperq9O\nKigabW6l0DI1YFLm3mPA73QvkkjbZnrKHMDCgJQDrz8yV820aBLKT4zUeuhq14r5\n7loRfHGG9I1xDFW63UT15E44LEsiEwArcPY0KTCH9Aktmp9gTr4wb5qCEJxdKWJW\nXzm3rMvWQZyxbd40IoKh\n=Y24P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:22:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/6d44d1fde6ec4c72ea21f2ffc6f0094b168e9468","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDZkNDRkMWZkZTZlYzRjNzJlYTIxZjJmZmM2ZjAwOTRiMTY4ZTk0Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61","sha":"64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec","sha":"c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec"}],"sha":"6d44d1fde6ec4c72ea21f2ffc6f0094b168e9468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/6d44d1fde6ec4c72ea21f2ffc6f0094b168e9468"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:09:55Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:09:55Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"fix(backup): refuse a miner key that is not the one this run is for\n\nThe runner encrypts whatever it finds at the expected path and names the\nartefact after the environment. micro-org#532: the estate mines from two\nhosts, the Deployment mounts the CLUSTER''s miner-keys over a hostPath,\nand for at least seventeen sets it wrote the k8s VM''s coinbase under the\nchain host''s name. Every path was correct. Every run was green. The key\nholding 112,011 EMBER was in none of them.\n\n`env.ts` already says the path is derived \"so a mainnet runner cannot be\npointed at the testnet key by a settings edit\". That is true and it was\nnot enough: it assumes the DIRECTORY is the right host''s. A path says\nwhere to look; only the address says what was found.\n\nBACKUP_MINER_EXPECTED_ADDRESS, optional, shape-checked at boot. On a\nmismatch no artefact is written and a warning names both addresses.\nRefusing rather than writing-with-a-warning is the whole point: run.ts\nsets `backup_secrets_included` from the artefact, so refusing is what\nmakes MinerCoinbaseKeyUnbacked fire — and its text is then true. Writing\nit anyway would leave the gauge at 1 and reproduce the silence.\n\nThe shape check lives beside ADDRESS_SHAPE in secrets.ts rather than in\nenv.ts, so the definition that validates a CONFIGURED address and the one\nthat reads an address out of a key file cannot drift.\n\nLeft unconfigured deliberately. Either value changes behaviour and the\nchoice is the owner''s: pinning the chain host''s address fires the alert\n(true, but the k8s VM''s dormant key then loses its only backup); pinning\nthe k8s VM''s locks in what is actually mounted but leaves 112,011 EMBER\nuncovered and silent. #532 has both options written out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"996e8555cd2f555134d7f7b9e5cfe6da60cf61e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/996e8555cd2f555134d7f7b9e5cfe6da60cf61e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGMxYjFlNmRmNmMzMzc4OWU5NjMxZTEzZDFjN2UwMDllYjUyNGJlZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61","sha":"64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61"}],"sha":"c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/c1b1e6df6c33789e9631e13d1c7e009eb524beec"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:39:48Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:39:48Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"runbooks: the custody master secret, which five documents already cited\n\n`.gitignore`, two runbooks and two docs all name `runbook-custody-master-secret.md` as\nthe remedy or the restore dependency, and it has never existed. micro-org#25 item 2.\n\nWritten from the mechanism rather than about it: the four-phase rotation is the one\n`custody/src/reencrypt.ts` documents in its own header, the verification is the query\nagainst `custody_keys_version_idx` rather than a log line, and the CLI''s non-zero exit\nis called out as the point — \"the command succeeding is the same statement as the old\nsecret can now be removed\".\n\nThe dangerous operation is named as what it is. Rotation is safe and restartable,\nbecause the pass writes the blob before the row and re-reads the blob''s own stamp;\nremoving an old secret on a partial run is what loses keys, and step 4 exists to make\nthat moment observable.\n\nIt also states the gap rather than leaving the reader to find it. Verified today: the\nnewest mainnet backup set records `custodyKeyringIncluded: false`, and its `secrets/`\nholds the miner key alone. The vault is backed up and the key that decrypts it is not —\nan availability problem, not a confidentiality one, and the last box on micro-org#25.\nThe reason it has stayed open is written down too: putting the KEK in the same set as\nthe ciphertext it protects defeats the purpose, so the fix is a design decision rather\nthan a configuration change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"625499b28c9f8956a0a85881ba1b453eb1b1ad8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/625499b28c9f8956a0a85881ba1b453eb1b1ad8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDY0YWIyMzQ1ZGRkMGRlMjU4ZGY2NTM2MjA1ZGIwNDFmZTI0NDVhNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626","sha":"d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626"}],"sha":"64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/64ab2345ddd0de258df6536205db041fe2445a61"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:04:58Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:04:58Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"README: what the estate actually is now — 17 Deployments, and agora is 23 modules\n\nThe Kubernetes banner was accurate and stopped short of the thing a reader most needs:\nthe shape. Below it the file still said \"the existing eighteen-container estate\", and\neverything after described a compose estate of roughly fifty services.\n\nTwo consolidations finished after the Kubernetes move — the network merge putting both\nestates in one namespace, and the service merge collapsing the over-split services into\n`agora` — and neither was visible from here. 17 application Deployments from 72 running\npods, listed per namespace, with the rule the survivors are separate under and pointers\nto the M5f disposition and to the two things that were refused: the `platform` rename,\nand M5e, which needs the owner.\n\nThe telemetry paragraph keeps its original claim and dates it, rather than quietly\nrestating the number: its six pods are outside the estate count on purpose, and M5f says\nwhy they are not a consolidation candidate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"c15470b82c24ddee777d34e93dc34609e1766028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/c15470b82c24ddee777d34e93dc34609e1766028"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGQ0Yzk1MTA0ZTNhMzAyMDUzYjg5NGVmNGQzMTNhNTg3NDMyZjk2MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565","sha":"a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565"}],"sha":"d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d4c95104e3a302053b894ef4d313a587432f9626"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T11:24:37Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T11:24:37Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"docs: the `app` database is dropped, and estate-verify has one standing failure now\n\nIt has failed since at least M5b: a database on the live server that `initdb.sql` does\nnot declare, so a rebuilt estate would come up without it. Measured before acting —\nzero relations across every non-system schema, zero functions, one extension\n(`plpgsql`, which every database has), zero connections, and no connection string\nanywhere in deploy, org or faucet naming it. Residue: created once, never written to.\n\nDropped rather than declared, which is the second half of the check''s own advice.\nDeclaring it would enshrine a database nothing uses, and a rebuilt estate has never had\nit — that is the proof it is not needed. The live server now has exactly the 52\ndatabases initdb.sql declares.\n\nRecorded here because the action is not in any file; it happened on the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"aa5bad3eb80dc870e477efc8cd492ed36cca7c8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/aa5bad3eb80dc870e477efc8cd492ed36cca7c8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGE5ZDliYzRlNzlhODNiY2EwNWNjZjViZjdkZTEyNjliOWM0YzE1NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165","sha":"dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165"}],"sha":"a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/a9d9bc4e79a83bca05ccf5bf7de1269b9c4c1565"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T11:22:15Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T11:22:15Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"estate-verify followed tessera''s frozen paths, which it was the first caller to miss\n\n2026.8.108 moved tessera''s `/v1/title` and `/v1/provision` under `/tessera`, so that\nNEITHER title answers the bare pair and a title registered at an origin-only base URL\n404s instead of being handed the wrong game. The gateway rewrites for public callers\nand `worlds` reads a registry row, so nothing outside was affected — but this file\ncalls the service directly, and five checks in its tessera section failed on 404.\n\nThat is the change working. It is also my omission: the aetherholm half of this got a\n`$AETHERHOLM_BASE` in 2026.8.107 and the tessera half did not get its `$TESSERA_BASE`\nin the same commit as the remount.\n\nOnly the TWO frozen paths move. `/v1/wards`, `/v1/parcels` and `/v1/discover` are\ntessera''s own and stay on `$TESSERA`.\n\nThe aetherholm comment is corrected with it: it said a bare `$AETHERHOLM/v1/provision`\n\"would now be answered by TESSERA\". True for exactly one release; the bare path is now\nanswered by nobody, which is the better failure and the reason for the second move.\n\n`k8s-estate-verify.sh` needs no change — it derives service URLs from the\n`VAR=${VAR:-http://127.0.0.1:${PB}NNN}` pattern, and `TESSERA_BASE` defaults off\n`$TESSERA` exactly as `AETHERHOLM_BASE` does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"7c4f6bb77e135a760796acd4b465916327224bd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/7c4f6bb77e135a760796acd4b465916327224bd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGRjMjI1ZmY0OGY5MTc5ODhkYzhiMTYyMGVhY2VlYTA1MjYwZjExNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5","sha":"d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5"}],"sha":"dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/dc225ff48f917988dc8b1620eaceea05260f1165"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:44:41Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:44:41Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"A sixth statement: where the running page sends its API calls\n\nThe five this file compared are LITERALS — registry, router, build, server, gateway —\nand they cover everything about a mount except the one thing a mounted page does most\noften. `apiBase()` is a derivation, so it was outside the table, and outside it a bundle\ncan resolve `''''` and send every `/v1/…` to the apex root. micro-site answers `text/html`\nthere, so each panel renders a failure state over an entirely green network tab: a\n200-shaped failure upstream of the mistake, which is this file''s stated subject.\n\nmicro-web-template shipped exactly that for the fortnight after wave 3 — it is the file\nevery new surface is scaffolded from, and it had no pushes for CI to run on.\n\nA SHAPE rather than a value, because `apiBase()` reads `window.location` and, on nine\nbundles, the reader''s chosen network too; there is nothing to compare against from here\nwithout a browser. Four shapes are recognised, which is four more than there should be —\ntask 207 collapses them, and this becomes one case when it does.\n\nThree path-mounted surfaces have no API base of their own: worlds-web reaches `api.<apex>`\n(a root surface, so no mount to carry), and exchange-web and journal-web call identity and\nnothing else. Declared with the key each really uses, checked in both directions like every\nother table here — a bundle that GAINS an own API base while sitting on that list would be\nexempted from the check that would have caught it.\n\nVerified by breaking trade-web: exit 1, naming the surface. web-template is NOT covered —\nit is a template, not a registry surface, so `BUNDLE_REPOS` cannot reach it; its own suite\ncarries the equivalent case now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"7ef8ea59b57f20fd65970d1818cc5640b22f8ef8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/7ef8ea59b57f20fd65970d1818cc5640b22f8ef8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGQ1MjJkZjFlN2ViMjMzMmJmNWIwMWNjMzI2Yjk0YjViYzFhYjc0ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3","sha":"60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3"}],"sha":"d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d522df1e7eb2332bf5b01cc326b94b5bc1ab74d5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:30:03Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:30:03Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"Render the estate at 2026.8.108\n\nManifests only — the same 9 mainnet and 1 testnet Deployments, re-pinned to the\ndigests `cfctl release 2026.8.108` recorded and re-verified.\n\nNOT YET APPLIED. The cluster has been unreachable from this workstation since\napproximately 09:45 today: ARP is incomplete for 192.168.1.171, .129 and .42, and a\nsweep of the segment finds six devices, none of them the estate''s. The estate itself\nis healthy and serving — cloudsforge.online 200, hub 401, status 200, the tunnel up —\nso this is the path from here, not the cluster. Applying is one command from a host\nthat can reach it:\n\n    ./scripts/k8s-deploy.sh --network mainnet   (then --network testnet)\n    ./scripts/k8s-gateway.sh --network mainnet  (then --network testnet)\n    ./scripts/k8s-estate-verify.sh              (ONCE — it spends mail quota)\n\nThere is no cutover SQL this time. tessera has no row in the `titles` registry, so\nunlike aetherholm''s in 2026.8.107 nothing has to move in step with the remount.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"b5c5d12fb340f451d7bc68524e772cbc1d0d68ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/b5c5d12fb340f451d7bc68524e772cbc1d0d68ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDYwYTc4MzAyYTc1NjM1YTkyMzEyNWYwM2NjOGNiMGMzZDI3YmY1YzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8","sha":"9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8"}],"sha":"60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/60a78302a75635a923125f03cc8cb0c3d27bf5c3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:41:02Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:41:02Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"docs: M5f — 17 application Deployments, and the `platform` rename refused\n\nThe audit that closes the wave sequence. It supersedes the 2026-08-28 disposition\nwhere the two disagree: that section concluded consolidation was complete at 31\nDeployments and then M5a–M5d absorbed twenty-two more services. Its rule was not\nwrong, it was applied to a candidate list that predated the trust-tier framing.\n\n17 application Deployments from 72 pods, read from the cluster rather than derived.\nThe registry agrees: 52 deployable rows, 30 releasable, 22 absorbed. Every survivor\nhas a one-line reason, and the rule is now about trust rather than coupling — a\nprocess that can issue a token, post to the ledger or sign a transaction shares\nitself with nothing.\n\nThe rename is refused on measurement: 47 `http://agora:4000` occurrences, 62 live\nsubscription rows across 25 databases that moved yesterday and would move again, 22\nExternalName targets. And the part that makes it not a rename at all — `AGORA_` is\none prefix for two things, the process''s own config and the social product''s rules,\ntold apart only by knowing what each variable means. That is a disentangling with a\nrename on the end of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"c8ea9f733f719fce7ebd1c6bc2bf12b22d0eeeec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/c8ea9f733f719fce7ebd1c6bc2bf12b22d0eeeec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDk1ODZjMmNjMGRmODkzMWY3YmE1MmI5MmFkY2ZhODZhMGJkMzA0Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49","sha":"9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49"}],"sha":"9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9586c2cc0df8931f7ba52b92adcfa86a0bd304f8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:37:32Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:37:32Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"tessera''s frozen title paths move too, so the bare pair answers nothing\n\nM5d moved aetherholm''s `/v1/title` and `/v1/provision` and left tessera''s bare, on\nthe usual rule: the module a caller already addresses keeps the path. That resolved\nthe collision and left a sharper edge behind it.\n\n`worlds` composes a title''s address from the pathname of its REGISTERED base URL plus\nthe frozen suffix. A row at an origin-only base — `http://agora:4000`, which is what\nevery row looked like before M5d and what a hand-written one looks like again — asks\nfor the bare `/v1/title`. While ONE title answered it, such a row got a 200 and the\nwrong game''s descriptor. A misconfigured registry row was indistinguishable from a\ncorrect one, and the only symptom was a player provisioned something they had not\nbought.\n\nWith both moved the bare path 404s: a row somebody fixes in a minute.\n\n`cf-tessera-title-contract`, anchored with `$` like aetherholm''s because only these two\npaths move, on both of tessera''s routers. `check-remount-rewrites.py` needed no edit —\nit derives the requirement from the module''s own REMOUNTED_PATHS, and went from\ndemanding 12 rewrites to 14 by itself.\n\ntessera has no row in the `titles` registry, so unlike aetherholm''s there is nothing to\nmigrate in this release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"36912c99f5cd17abb0c6f21ed17e6e102cf5b747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/36912c99f5cd17abb0c6f21ed17e6e102cf5b747"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDlhMmJkMmEwMzBiMzZiNjJmOWUwYTU1NTAzZjEwZmFmY2ExNWZmNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c","sha":"1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c"}],"sha":"9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/9a2bd2a030b36b62f9e0a55503f10fafca15ff49"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:48:36Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:48:36Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"CI checks out micro-agora, and the sibling guard can see a pathlib read\n\n`check-remount-rewrites.py` reads every module''s REMOUNTED_PATHS out of the agora\ncheckout and REFUSES rather than skips when it is absent — a check that cannot run\nreports failure, not a success it did not establish. The drift job never checked\nagora out, so the guard was red from the first push of the wave that wrote it.\n\nThe reason nothing said so is a hole in `check-sibling-prerequisites.py`: it looked\nfor `../<name>/` string literals, and that script opens the sibling as\n`MICRO / \"agora\" / \"src\"`. No literal, no reference, clean report. It now also reads\nthe pathlib spelling — `ROOT.parent / \"x\"` and any constant assigned from\n`ROOT.parent` — anchored on `ROOT.parent` specifically, because a looser `.parent`\nmatched `ROOT / \"Makefile\"` and reported this repository''s own Makefile as a missing\nsibling.\n\nWith that, it names agora, which is now a REQUIRED row in SIBLING_TABLE: a fresh host\nneeds it for the same reason CI does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"5da1334440c58b6347148ed245cbfeaff775eba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/5da1334440c58b6347148ed245cbfeaff775eba2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDFjOWNhY2VhMDIwMmY3Yjc3NTE5MTBmN2RiZTNhYTQzM2YyZmRmMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c","sha":"f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c"}],"sha":"1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/1c9cacea0202f7b7751910f7dbe3aa433f2fdf2c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:37:10Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:37:10Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"docs: M5d deployed — estate 18 → 13 Deployments, and the two things it got wrong\n\nBoth networks applied, both gateways rolled, five absorbed Deployments pruned, 62\nsubscription rows moved across 25 databases with none left behind. Verified through\nthe public edge. estate-verify: the same 2 pre-existing failures as M5b and M5c.\n\nRecorded with the two mid-flight findings rather than without them: the migrate Job''s\nmissing MARKET_URL, and aetherholm''s frozen title paths answering as tessera through\na gateway the exemption said they never reached.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"3057a58577d81d01ede031fb71dcd999081e1572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/3057a58577d81d01ede031fb71dcd999081e1572"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGY2MjlkMDc3OWQzZWRiYTkxMDQ0NzlkNmQwMmI0ODBhNWFhMmE3N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98","sha":"272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98"}],"sha":"f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/f629d0779d3edba9104479d6d02b480a5aa2a77c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:31:45Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:31:45Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"aetherholm''s frozen title paths need a gateway rewrite after all\n\nThe M5d exemption said `worlds` computes a title''s address from its registered base\nURL, so no request for `/v1/title` or `/v1/provision` passes through Traefik. True of\nworlds, false of the estate: two routers here carry `/v1` for that title, and minutes\nafter the gateway rolled,\n\n    GET https://<apex>/worlds/aetherholm/v1/title  ->  200, body named TESSERA\n\n`cf-aetherholm-title-contract` rewrites exactly those two paths — anchored with `$`,\nbecause aetherholm''s other twenty-seven stay bare — and it is attached to both\nrouters, after the strip on the apex one so it sees the path it is written against.\n\nThe checker changes with it, in the two places that let the hole through:\n\n  * the exemption is DELETED rather than reworded;\n  * a frozen constant it cannot resolve is now a FAILURE. It used to print \"value\n    lives in contracts; pair exists\" and pass, which is how a remounted path went a\n    release with nothing routed to it. The values are read out of the contracts\n    checkout — the one package both titles import them from — rather than mirrored\n    here, where a copy would agree with itself for ever.\n\nVerified in both directions: detaching the middleware fails the check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"c7caa41a6f04a0e7022ab7df9337093508a1c932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/c7caa41a6f04a0e7022ab7df9337093508a1c932"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDI3MjE1OGMwNjYyMWFjMTk2OThiNGNiOTU4NjhlYTdhOTQ5MDRjOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8","sha":"bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8"}],"sha":"272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/272158c06621ac19698b4cb95868ea7a94904c98"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:23:00Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:23:00Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"M5d: the migrator needs MARKET_URL, because env.ts validates the whole config\n\nWave 30 refused with `admin-api  step=env  MARKET_URL is required`. A migrator does\nnot call market — but `agora/src/migrator.ts` imports `admin/module.ts` for its\nmigration targets, and every `env.ts` validates the WHOLE config at import, not the\npart the caller is about to use. The four peer URLs already in this Job are there\nfor the same reason and none of them is dialled either.\n\nNothing downstream was applied, so the estate was unchanged: the failure cost a\ndeploy, not an outage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"4e4c2a783ab15db9d3eea217ca0e98373b4199cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/4e4c2a783ab15db9d3eea217ca0e98373b4199cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGJhZDAwMzFkNDdiOTczYmRjNmJmOWI5MTBlNzBkOTkxY2JjMmZkYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90","sha":"adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90"}],"sha":"bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/bad0031d47b973bdc6bf9b910e70d991cbc2fdb8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:16:03Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T17:16:03Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"M5d: hub-api, trade, wallet, admin-api and emberkin become agora (2026.8.107)\n\nFive more `MERGED_INTO` entries, and `nda`/`aetherholm` re-pointed from `emberkin`\nto the end of their chain. The estate renders 9 mainnet Deployments where it\nrendered 14, and 23 ExternalName aliases keep every service-to-service name\nresolving. cloudsforge-estate goes 18 → 13.\n\nTHE GATEWAY HALF. A remount inside the process is only half of it: the bytes on the\nwire still say the bare path. Three replacePathRegex middlewares carry what moved —\nhub''s whole `/v1/*` surface to `/v1/hub/*`, admin''s worlds family to\n`/v1/operator/worlds*`, and tessera''s `/v1/listings*` (the M5b regression, #193).\n`check-remount-rewrites.py` derives the requirement from each module''s own\n`REMOUNTED_PATHS` rather than a list, so the next wave cannot forget it; it was\nproven to fail in both directions before being wired into CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qrn6FFp59sqq2bgnq6qz2E","tree":{"sha":"e0cf2c8721bbf39ac7e1710c87a5e429e35167d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/e0cf2c8721bbf39ac7e1710c87a5e429e35167d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGFkZjMyYzY1OWUwMjFlZWEwN2ZkNjNkYjE0M2ZjZjk1ZjE5ZGFkOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc","sha":"d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc"}],"sha":"adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/adf32c659e021eea07fd63db143fcf95f19dad90"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:20:11Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:20:11Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"docs: M5c shipped (release 2026.8.106), estate 20→18 Deployments — under the target\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc4a90ab76e134f8877038941f82c660502058e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/dc4a90ab76e134f8877038941f82c660502058e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGQ2OGY4NWUzM2Q3ZTM4NTE3OGM2ZDM3NzM4ZWNkYWJjZWNkYzM1Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1","sha":"bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1"}],"sha":"d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/d68f85e33d7e385178c6d37738ecdabcecdc35cc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:08:07Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:08:07Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"M5c: agora absorbs activity and lantern (release 2026.8.106)\n\nThe bus tail and the telemetry sink join the platform monolith (micro-agora#9,\nmicro-org#527). Both were already absorbers themselves — notify merged into\nactivity at M2, analytics into lantern at M1 — so this wave adds FOUR modules\nand agora reaches sixteen. 16 Deployments become 14.\n\ncompose:\n  * agora gains the four databases, notify''s mail pipeline and lantern''s RUM\n    origins and tokens; env_file gains the analytics pepper file. agora-migrate\n    mirrors them, because `src/migrator.ts` imports every module and each\n    `env.ts` validates at import — the M5b lesson, restated by agora''s own CI\n    migrate job.\n  * activity, lantern and their two migrators are DELETED, along with the M2\n    prose that described notify''s absorption into a service that no longer\n    exists. depends_on repaired (beacon, hub-api already named agora).\n\nTHE MAIL PIPELINE IS NOW IN THE PLATFORM, and that is written down rather than\n  left implicit: an RCE in any platform route table reaches SMTP_*. It is inside\n  the owner''s trust-tier decision (plan §M5); identity, ledger and the vault stay\n  out so the same bug cannot also mint, rewrite the book, or sign.\nTHE ANALYTICS PEPPER comes too. `ANALYTICS_PSEUDONYM_KEY` cannot be drained —\n  lookup_key is HMAC(pepper, subject) and the subject is never stored — so it\n  stays the analytics module''s own and its boundary guard now scans every file\n  agora compiles.\n\nk8s-render.py MERGED_INTO: activity and lantern -> agora. These LENGTHEN two\n  existing chains, which is safe because `merge_target()` follows merges to the\n  end: the render emits notify and analytics as ExternalNames straight at agora,\n  not as CNAME hops through names with no pod. Verified in the output.\n\ngateway: cf-svc-lantern and cf-api-activity re-pointed at agora:4000.\nerasure: activity and notify move host; analytics moves host AND path — its bare\n  /ingest is remounted /ingest/analytics so the three signed inboxes are distinct.\n\nk8s/estate/{mainnet,testnet}/ re-rendered from 2026.8.106; check-k8s green; all\ntwelve deploy checks pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef6bc6ad8f3c99200ba49da9b68d83f60336f7d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/ef6bc6ad8f3c99200ba49da9b68d83f60336f7d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGJkODM0NmJhMjUwOTMxNGQwZDBlODIxN2YyZWNiOWNiMDUwNzYyYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1","sha":"71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1"}],"sha":"bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/bd8346ba2509314d0d0e8217f2ecb9cb050762a1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:38:50Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:38:50Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"docs: M5b shipped (release 2026.8.105), estate 27→20 Deployments\n\nRecords the live verification and the two lessons that will recur: the merged\nmigrator needs the modules'' upstream URLs (each env.ts validates at import), and\nthe merged suite flakes because more test files share each module''s one test\ndatabase — fix isolation before M5d.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b2e55feb16cb691488db53af3d5d90da8865f00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/7b2e55feb16cb691488db53af3d5d90da8865f00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDcxYTBlZDg0ZTg1ODA5OWZiMjAzODdlYTFkOTZlODQ5MDg3ZGJhZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384","sha":"43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384"}],"sha":"71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/71a0ed84e858099fb20387ea1d96e849087dbad1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:26:46Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:26:46Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"M5b: agora-migrate needs the modules'' upstream URLs, not just their DSNs\n\nThe 2026.8.105 deploy failed at wave 30: `community … LEDGER_BASE_URL is\nrequired`, three attempts, nothing downstream applied. A migrator calls no\nupstream, but `src/migrator.ts` IMPORTS every module and a module''s env.ts\nvalidates at import, so community''s `required(source,''LEDGER_BASE_URL'')` throws\nbefore any migration runs. agora''s own CI migrate job sets this same set beside\nthe twelve DSNs — it is the authority for what the merged migrator reads, and\nthis block had only the DSNs. Mirrors the runtime block, as lantern-migrate\nmirrors lantern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01b88dcaf474af99656ee7e55c3b7b4b9904ba77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/01b88dcaf474af99656ee7e55c3b7b4b9904ba77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDQzYzcxNzNlMTA2Yjk0YWZkMTViMTNmOWI4OGRiMTZjMzRhZTIzODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd","sha":"0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd"}],"sha":"43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/43c7173e106b94afd15b13f9b88db16c34ae2384"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:23:16Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T08:23:16Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"M5b: agora absorbs the commerce/games tier (release 2026.8.105)\n\nSeven more modules — community, market, billing, mint, foresight, worlds,\ntessera — join the platform monolith (micro-agora#8, micro-org#526). Twelve\nmodules in one process; 23 Deployments become 16.\n\ncompose:\n  * agora gains the seven databases, their upstream URLs, one identity\n    credential each, and mint''s/foresight''s own settings. `PORT` is deliberately\n    NOT carried: foresight set 4021 and tessera 4022, and in the merged process\n    there is one listener on 4000 — the render confirms PORT=4000.\n  * env_file gains env/chain.<network>.env (foresight''s EVM settings, which mint\n    shares) and the block gains extra_hosts for host.docker.internal. The outbox\n    secret file already carries COMMUNITY_INGEST_SECRETS and tessera''s\n    INBOUND_SIGNING_SECRET, still held apart from OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET.\n  * agora-migrate now migrates all twelve databases in one pass.\n  * the seven services and their seven migrators are DELETED (929 lines), and\n    every dangling depends_on repointed to agora or deduped where agora was\n    already named. `docker compose config` is valid: 36 long-running, 16 one-shot.\n\nk8s-render.py MERGED_INTO: seven more ExternalName aliases. The M4a port trap is\n  disarmed rather than ignored — as modules they mount into agora''s 4000, and a\n  grep proved nothing but four gateway upstreams and one erasure row ever named\n  :4021/:4022. All are re-pointed here.\n\ngateway: ten upstreams re-pointed at agora:4000 across estate-web and public-api.\nerasure/register.psv: market, billing, tessera, mint, community moved to their\n  split /v1/events/<module> paths at agora (the bare path 410s post-merge).\ndocs: M5b recorded, including the tessera/aetherholm frozen-contract-path\n  collision that becomes REAL at M5d and must be split there.\n\nk8s/estate/{mainnet,testnet}/ re-rendered from 2026.8.105; check-k8s green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc1579a6185c29c45d3955d7ec0537f06cea95c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/dc1579a6185c29c45d3955d7ec0537f06cea95c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDBlNTIwNjhhOTk2M2YyNGNmNmYyOGZhNWY3MTQzYzMyMWEwNzE4ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d","sha":"0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d"}],"sha":"0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/0e52068a9963f24cf6f28fa5f7143c321a0718fd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T16:16:27Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T16:16:27Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"docs: M5a shipped (release 2026.8.104), estate 50→46 — record the live verification\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bfbab848c0ea15f8e07952474b623e0883ac8134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/bfbab848c0ea15f8e07952474b623e0883ac8134"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDBmOWVkZjEzMjk2MmI1MmJiMWZlMzgwMDJhYmYxNDlkNDBjNzI2NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda","sha":"ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda"}],"sha":"0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/0f9edf132962b52bb1fe38002abf149d40c7265d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T16:13:50Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T16:13:50Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"estate-verify: cfx execs the absorber''s Deployment, not the pruned one\n\nAfter a wave-M merge the absorbed service''s Deployment is gone, so\n`kubectl exec deploy/<absorbed>` hits nothing and every command ''succeeds''\nempty — which is how the studio content-address check read as ''a green with no\nbytes'' after M5a even though studio-in-agora had written the file. The k8s\nwrapper now emits CF_MERGED_INTO (the absorbed->absorber map it already computes\nfor URL resolution) and cfx/cfx_in chase it to a fixpoint before exec. No-op\nunder compose, where every absorbed service still has its own container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b01b19f2c684ca5bd1251d4bb034b7166d44bfb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/b01b19f2c684ca5bd1251d4bb034b7166d44bfb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGVlMGRmNjdmY2MxY2IxNTk4NGRiMmE5NTQ2OWExYmIzMjQzNDRiZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377","sha":"aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377"}],"sha":"ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/ee0df67fcc1cb15984db2a95469a1bb324344bda"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T15:56:11Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T15:56:11Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"M5a: agora absorbs devplatform/policy/pricing/studio (release 2026.8.104)\n\nThe platform-monolith seed. agora''s image (micro-agora#7) now runs all four\nmodules; this is the deploy-side cutover.\n\ncompose:\n  * agora runs five databases (its own + the four modules''), mounts the\n    studio-assets PVC (renderer stamps Recreate), and agora-migrate migrates all\n    five in one pass. The four services and their four migrators are DELETED.\n  * dangling depends_on repointed to the absorber: policy/pricing/studio -> agora\n    across custody, wallet, market, trade, community, tessera, foresight, hub-api;\n    hub-api''s now-duplicate policy and its M2-residue notify (-> activity, already\n    present) deduped. `docker compose config` is valid again.\n\nk8s-render.py MERGED_INTO: devplatform/policy/pricing/studio -> agora (four\n  transparent 4000->4000 ExternalName aliases); k8s/estate/{mainnet,testnet}/\n  re-rendered from 2026.8.104 — agora on sha256:60b17a…, the four Deployments\n  gone, aliases present. check-k8s green.\n\ngateway: cf-api-pricing, cf-api-devplatform, cf-svc-devplatform, cf-svc-studio\n  re-pointed at agora.\ntiers.yaml: agora -> Tier 1 (inherits pricing/policy).\nerasure/register.psv: policy/devplatform/agora rows moved to the split\n  /v1/events/{policy,devplatform,agora} paths (bare path 410s post-merge).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af64f474f8123ce3852336627d0d412bba8a1d6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/af64f474f8123ce3852336627d0d412bba8a1d6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKGFlZWJkYzIzY2ExM2RhMWMyN2NlZTM1ZmVmMjNkYzUwY2RhNDIzNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/68c5d124b582ef360b718621eb5558d824637718","sha":"68c5d124b582ef360b718621eb5558d824637718","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/68c5d124b582ef360b718621eb5558d824637718"}],"sha":"aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/aeebdc23ca13da1c27cee35fef23dc50cda42377"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4446752?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/savvaniss/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/savvaniss/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/savvaniss/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/savvaniss/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/savvaniss","id":4446752,"login":"savvaniss","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NDY3NTI=","organizations_url":