ts/5ef34d056b02e7e3c1666d6cd18aa3dbe14d3b11"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commits/2a4c4beb42b6ff7ffcb8c195c831748bbe6215c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:10:46Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:10:46Z","email":"spyridon-efstathios.savvanis.ext@daiichisankyo.com","name":"Savvanis Spyros"},"message":"docs: the disposition of every remaining service\n\nConsolidation is complete, not paused. Every backend service has been\nassessed against a stated rule and has a recorded disposition, so this\ndoes not need re-deriving next quarter.\n\nThe rule came out of the evidence rather than being assumed. The plan''s\nhard-exclusion list already contained it, stated for settlement alone and\nnever generalised: merging widens the set of code paths that can reach a\nbroadcast. Measured across the fourteen remaining candidates, the same\nsentence applies to ledger.postEntry, and nine of them hold it.\n\nOf the five that do not: pricing polls third-party HTTP feeds, studio\nowns a PVC, policy has no partner, and devplatform+agora is the closest\ncall in the estate — structurally clean, refused because it is the only\ncandidate with no shared domain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85984662e2fa44c728faac7e80a7b232693fc0cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/trees/85984662e2fa44c728faac7e80a7b232693fc0cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/git/commits/2a4c4beb42b6ff7ffcb8c195c831748bbe6215c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudsforge-online/micro-deploy/commit/2a4c4beb42b6ff7ffcb8c195c831748bbe6215c2","node_id":"C_kwDOTokGJNoAKDJhNGM0YmViNDJiNmZmN2ZmY2I4YzE5NWM4MzE