nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sairamg8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sairamg8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sairamg8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sairamg8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sairamg8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sairamg8/frontendbible.github.io/commits/97eb2da3b69c1cfe179a202d93678f28853990ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T03:21:16Z","email":"sairamgudiputi8@gmail.com","name":"sairamgudiputi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T03:21:16Z","email":"sairamgudiputi8@gmail.com","name":"sairamgudiputi"},"message":"fix: remove duplicate Vite SPA, fix production build crash\n\nThe Vite SPA (src/App.tsx + index.html + vite.config.ts) had reappeared\nas a second, hand-rolled documentation UI competing with Docusaurus, with\npackage.json''s build script repointed at `vite build`. Removed it and all\nits assets/tsconfig scaffolding, trimming package.json back to\nDocusaurus-only deps and restoring `build` -> `docusaurus build`.\n\nAlso fixes a real, previously-never-verified `yarn build` crash\n(`TypeError: require.resolveWeak is not a function` in the SSR bundle):\npackage.json''s `\"type\": \"module\"` combined with Docusaurus''s Node-version-\nderived webpack server target broke react-loadable''s require.resolveWeak\ncodegen. Removing `\"type\": \"module\"` fixes it.\n\nSwitched Yarn from PnP to the node-modules linker (.yarnrc.yml), which\ndrops the generated .pnp.cjs/.pnp.loader.mjs and the PnP-runtime-polluted\nwebpack disk cache that had been committed. Moved the one real favicon\nfrom Vite''s public/ to Docusaurus''s static/img/.","tree":{"sha":"f8abc83b95fd0ce33b9f4ad86139b33f191fe071","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sairamg8/frontendbible.github.io/git/trees/f8abc83b95fd0ce33b9f4ad86139b33f191fe071"},"url":"https://api.gi