a46b56e19493f194a72b5e99d10e5f97137853e7"}],"sha":"a2c281194bd4feb491723b88bd89a09ca5050063","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commits/a2c281194bd4feb491723b88bd89a09ca5050063"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commits/a46b56e19493f194a72b5e99d10e5f97137853e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:58:27Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T08:58:27Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: cap branch titles by display columns; repair a hollow test (DEF-18/19/20)\n\nRound-5 adversarial review of 64294d1 - the first pass over code that\nlanded after the gauntlet closed. Three lenses, three DO-NOT-SHIP, three\nMAJORs each corroborated by two reviewers using different methods.\n\nDEF-18 reopened: the cap counted UTF-16 code units while the defect is\nmeasured in pixels. Sixty Han glyphs render at 851-862px - at or above\nthe 850px that filed it - and ''请''*60 was not truncated at all, since\nlength > 60 is false. Kimi is Moonshot AI''s CLI, so a Chinese auto-title\nis the expected case, and both new tests were blind to it: no truncation\nemits no ellipsis, so they stayed green while the panel was broken.\nThe budget is now in DISPLAY COLUMNS in src/label.ts - wide characters\nand emoji count 2, iteration is by code point (which also removes the\nlone-surrogate split) - and the module is JupyterLab-free so jest can\nexecute it, the same treatment colour.ts already had.\n\nDEF-19: `two different branches open as two independent terminals` had\nbeen hollow since 9917983. page.locator(''.lm-Menu'').last() resolves to\nthe ROOT menu until Lumino''s ~366ms open delay elapses, and the root''s\ncommand items are visible, so it clicked Resume and Resume (YOLO) -\nconfirmed from the Playwright trace of a green run showing two\nlaunch-terminal POSTs for the id the API names `current`. It would have\npassed with _openBranch deleted, and it was the sole evidence behind a\nclosed acceptance criterion. Now gated on the submenu attaching, and\nasserted against the recorded launch payloads rather than a terminal\ncount that cannot tell a resume from a branch. Mutation-proven.\n\nDEF-20: the Manage Sessions popup never ellipsised - no max-width, and\nJupyterLab''s .jp-Dialog-content caps at an absolute 1000px, so the\ndialog widened to ~955px rather than the label shrinking. The round-4\nfix asserted the opposite in three places it touched; all corrected.\n\n70 jest, 152 pytest, 10 Galata, tsc exit 0, eslint 0 errors.","tree":{"sha":"7a0d975dc154f39c480a80ed9c98b5ab30c71e85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/git/trees/7a0d975dc154f39c480a80ed9c98b5ab30c71e85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/git/commits/a46b56e19493f194a72b5e99d10e5f97137853e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commit/a46b56e19493f194a72b5e99d10e5f97137853e7","node_id":"C_kwDOTpjRh9oAKGE0NmI1NmUxOTQ5M2YxOTRhNzJiNWU5OWQxMGU1Zjk3MTM3ODUzZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commit/64294d1193de9981a2d6450ce862aa0105fa93b6","sha":"64294d1193de9981a2d6450ce862aa0105fa93b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commits/64294d1193de9981a2d6450ce862aa0105fa93b6"}],"sha":"a46b56e19493f194a72b5e99d10e5f97137853e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commits/a46b56e19493f194a72b5e99d10e5f97137853e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commits/64294d1193de9981a2d6450ce862aa0105fa93b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:29:01Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:29:01Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: cap branch titles in the context submenus (DEF-18)\n\nFound by a live smoke test against real ~/.kimi-code storage, not by the\nsuite. Kimi auto-titles a session from its first prompt, so a routine\n139-character title rendered a branch submenu 850px wide - covering the\nfile browser and terminal. Lumino sets no max-width on\n.lm-Menu-itemLabel, and the Manage Sessions popup had truncated the same\nstring via CSS all along; the two menu paths were missed.\n\n_branchMenuLabel caps the title at BRANCH_MENU_TITLE_MAX for the two\nLumino submenus only. The popup keeps the full string for its CSS\nellipsis, and the aria-label keeps it for screen readers. Only the title\nis trimmed - the short id and relative time are what distinguish two\nbranches of the same project, so truncating the composed label would\nhave traded a cosmetic defect for a functional one. Re-measured live:\n850px -> 492px.\n\nVerification:\n- jest pin mutation-tested: reverting one of the two call sites fails it\n- Galata fixture now seeds a paragraph-length title; short-title\n  fixtures are why nine flows passed over this for four review rounds\n- new Galata flow asserts the ellipsis, the surviving id/time suffix,\n  and a width bound framed as a regression guard between the measured\n  850px and 600/492px populations\n\n69 jest, 152 pytest, 10 Galata, tsc exit 0, eslint 0 errors.","tree":{"sha":"72c470fe789f85645acf1bfb67391d38f902f64b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/git/trees/72c470fe789f85645acf1bfb67391d38f902f64b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/git/commits/64294d1193de9981a2d6450ce862aa0105fa93b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","