https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/commits/2165983084bfdde40bd2618348c8dc5ae5f95794/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T15:25:40Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T15:25:40Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"docs: record round-4 adversarial verdicts as DEF-15/16/17\n\nRound 4 confirmed all six round-3 edits sound across three lenses. The\nthree new findings were verified refute-by-default before any action:\n\n- DEF-15: the section-header focus ring was rendered in headless chromium\n  and shows a complete ring on all four edges. The header is a native\n  button inside .jp-ThemedContainer, so JupyterLab''s own buttons.css\n  already covers it; the proposed rule is dead CSS at lower specificity\n  and produced a byte-identical screenshot.\n- DEF-16: the claim that _deleteBranches held the file''s only silent\n  refresh catch fails a full census - five of nine sites are silent,\n  three of them with a comment explaining why.\n- DEF-17: the _pendingRefresh field comment is incomplete, not false;\n  it asserts no exclusivity and both neighbouring comments state the\n  two-path delivery correctly.\n\nRecorded so a later round cannot re-litigate them. No code changed.","tree":{"sha":"e8ede598b8188b768a1f95159d94709b9ae3c146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/git/trees/e8ede598b8188b768a1f95159d94709b9ae3c146"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_kimi_code_extension/git/commits/2165983084bfdde40bd2618348c8dc5ae5f95794","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/fo